$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: tert-Butyl
4-(5-((Benzylamino)methyl)-2-(methylthio)-pyrimidin-4-ylamino)cyclohexylcarbamate
(8a). General procedure for syntheses of 8a-v. Benzylamine (1 g, 9.25
mmol) and AcOH (0.1 mL) were added at room temperature to a solution of
7a (2.26 g, 6.17 mmol) in MeOH (50 mL). After the amine was converted
completely to the imine, NaBH4 (469 mg, 12.34 mmol) was added to the
reaction mixture at 0°C. The resulting mixture was concentrated in vacuo,
partitioned between CH2Cl2 and saturated NaHCO3, and extracted with
CH2Cl2. The organic layer was separated, washed with brine, dried with
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The resulting crude material
was subjected to flash column chromatography (SiO2, petroleum
ether/EtOAc, 3:1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design, Synthesis, and Biological Evaluation of
2-Oxo-3,4-dihydropyrimido[4,5 d]pyrimidinyl Derivatives as New
Irreversible Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor Inhibitors with Improved
Pharmacokinetic Properties
