$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-[5-(2-Fluorophenyl)-1-(pyridin-3-ylsulfonyl)-1H-pyrrol-3-yl]-N-methylmethanamine
Fumarate (13e). Compound 12f (1.52 g, 8.03 mmol) was dissolved in
methanol (30 mL). A 40% methylamine methanol solution (3.57 g, 35.0 mmol)
was added at room temperature, and the mixture was stirred for 30 min.
Sodium borohydride (523 mg, 13.8 mmol) was added at room temperature, and
the mixture was stirred for 10 min. Then 1 mol/L hydrochloric acid (50
mL) was added and the mixture was stirred for 5 min. The reaction mixture
was basified with a saturated aqueous sodium hydrogen carbonate solution,
and the mixture was extracted with ethyl acetate. The extract was washed
with brine, dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by basic silica gel column
chromatography (ethyl acetate-methanol, 1:0 to 7:3) to give 1.30 g of a
free base of the title compound as a pale-yellow oil. The obtained free
base (750 mg) was dissolved in ethyl acetate (30 mL). A solution of
fumaric acid (278 mg, 2.40 mmol) in methanol (3 mL) was added dropwise at
room temperature. After the mixture was stirred for 30 min, the obtained
crystals were collected by filtration and washed with ethyl acetate.
1-[5-(2-Fluorophenyl)-1-(pyridin-3-ylsulfonyl)-1H-pyrrol-3-yl]-N-methylmethanamine
Fumarate (13e) as colorless crystals, yield 912 mg, 74%. mp 201-203 °C.
1H NMR (DMSO-d6) δ: 2.43 (s, 3H), 3.87 (s, 2H), 6.47 (s, 2H), 6.49 (d, J
= 1.8 Hz, 1H), 7.07-7.13 (m, 1H), 7.19-7.26 (m, 2H), 7.49-7.56 (m, 1H),
7.59-7.64 (m, 1H), 7.74 (d, J = 1.8 Hz, 1H), 7.86-7.90 (m, 1H), 8.56-8.57
(m, 1H), 8.87-8.89 (m, 1H), 3H not detected. Anal. (C21H20FN3O6S),
Calculated: C, 54.66; H, 4.37; N, 9.11. Found: C, 54.70; H, 4.34; N,
9.07.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM dropwise addn. of fumaric acid (stage 5, substage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of a Novel Pyrrole Derivative
1-[5-(2-Fluorophenyl)-1-(pyridin-3-ylsulfonyl)-1H-pyrrol-3-yl]-N-methylmethanamine
Fumarate (TAK-438) as a Potassium-Competitive Acid Blocker (P-CAB)
