$DATUM 1-((1S,5R)-6,6-Dimethylbicyclo[3.1.1]hept-2-en-2-yl)-N-methylmethanamine
(9) Aldehyde 11 (2.00 g, 13.31 mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (40 mL). Then,
MeNH2 (33 % in EtOH/ca. 8 M, 4.0 mL, 32.1 mmol) was added. After 1 h of
stirring at r.t., imine formation was complete (NMR). NaBH4 (0.856 g,
22.63 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred under N2
atmosphere for 2 h at r.t.. The mixture was quenched by addition of
aqueous NaOH (2.5 M). Volatiles were evaporated in vacuo. DCM and brine
were added and the layers were separated. The aqueous layer was extracted
with DCM. The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4, filtered
and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by SPE on
Si-propylsulphonic acid material (wash with MeOH, elution with 7 N NH3 in
MeOH). This afforded the product. Brown oil, yield 1.10 g, 50%. 1H-NMR
(CDCl3, 250 MHz) δ (ppm) 5.36-5.30 (m, 1H), 3.06-3.01 (m, 2H), 2.37 (s,
3H), 2.37 - 2.31 (m, 1H), 2.27- 2.17 (m, 2H), 2.10-2.02 (m, 2H), 1.25 (s,
3H), 1.14 (d, 1H, J=8.6 Hz), 0.82 (s, 3H). LR-MS: m/z [M+H]+ = 166.05.
LC-purity (210 nm) = 92%.
