(0.348 g) was dissolved in a mixture of MeOH (0.7 mL) and THF (3.3 mL).
After silica gel column chromatography (1:5 ethyl acetate−n-hexane), pure
N-propylbenzyl amine (0.468 g) was obtained as a colorless oil (80%).
N-Methylcyclohexylamine. N-Methylcyclohexylamine was prepared according
to general procedure for reductive amination with cyclohexanone (0.464 g)
dissolved in a mixture of MeOH (1.31 mL) and THF (3.91 mL), and to methyl
