$DATUM N α -Methyl-trans-4-N-Fmoc-amino-L-proline-NH2 (9). To a solution of 8
(0.465 g, 0.001 mol) dissolved in MeOH (20 mL) at 0 °C were added a 37%
formaldehyde solution (0.812 g, 0.745 mL, 0.01 mol), NaBH3CN (0.314 g,
0.005 mol), and acetic acid (0.120 g, 0.115 mL, 0.002 mol). The reaction
mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight. The solvent was
evaporated under reduced pressure. The residue was dissolved in 5% NaHCO3
(10 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (10 mL × 3). The combined organic layers
were washed with brine and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified
by silica gel column chromatography (CH2Cl2:MeOH ) 9.5:0.5) to afford a
white solid (0.365 g, quantitative yield): 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ
(7.897 + 7.881) (d, 2H, J = 8 Hz), (7.694 + 7.680) (d, 2H, J = 7 Hz),
7.412 (t, 2H, J = 8 Hz), 7.331 (t, 2H, J = 7.5 Hz), (4.316 + 4.302) (d,
2H, J = 7 Hz), 4.204 (t, 1H, J = 7 Hz), 4.108-3.960 (m, 1H), 3.191 (t,
1H, J = 7 Hz), 2.781 (t, 1H, J = 8 Hz), 2.236 (s, 3H), 2.140 (t, 1H, J =
8.5 Hz), 1.986-1.896 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (125.7 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 174.9 (1C),
155.7 (1C), 143.9 (2C), 140.8 (2C), 127.6 (2C), 127.1 (2C), 125.2 (2C),
120.2 (2C), 67.6 (1C), 65.2 (1C), 61.1 (1C), 48.9 (1C), 46.7 (1C), 40.9
(1C), 36.7 (1C); ESI (CH3CN) m/z = 366.6 ([M + H]+).
