$DATUM 1-(Dimethylaminomethyl)cyclohexaneacetic Acid (4a) and
1-(Dimethylaminomethyl)-cyclohexaneacetic Acid Hydrochloride (4b). To a
solution of 1-(aminomethyl)-cyclohexaneacetic acid (1, 15.0 g, 87.7 mmol)
in methanol (900 mL) was added 37% aqueous form aldehyde (15 mL, 185.0
mmol) and 10% Pd/C (1.73 g). The reaction mixture was stirred at 25°C
under H2 gas (15 psi) for 5 h, the catalyst was removed by filtration
through celite, and the filtrate was concentrated in vacuo to dryness.
The residue was recrystallized from a mixture of acetone-hexanes.
1-(Dimethylaminomethyl)cyclohexaneacetic Acid (4a). Yield: (17.11 g, 98%
), colorless needle shaped crystals. mp 88-90°C ; 1H NMR (D2O): δ
1.20-1.55 (m, 10H, cyclohexyl H-2, H-3, H-4, H-5, H-6), 2.52 (s, 2H,
CH2CO2H), 2.82 (s, 6H, NMe2), 3.05 (s, 2H, CH2NMe2).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
