$DATUM N,N-Dimethyl-(3,7,9,9-tetramethyltricyclo[3.3.1.03,7]non-1-yl)amine
(2R,3R)-tartrate, 25·(2R,3R)-tartrate. A mixture of amine 18 (0.15 g, 0.8
mmol), NaBH3CN (0.15 g, 2.3 mmol), formaldehyde (0.20 mL, 37% in aqueous
solution, 2.4 mmol), acetic acid (0.1 mL) in MeOH (6 mL) with a CaCl2
tube was stirred at room temperature for 8 h. More NaBH3CN (0.15 g, 2.3
mmol) and formaldehyde (0.20 mL, 37% in aqueous solution, 2.4 mmol) were
added and the reaction was stirred at room temperature overnight. Then,
the reaction was concentrated under vacuo. The residue was dissolved in
H2O (7 mL) and the aqueous layer was basified with a solution of NaOH 10N
(3 mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (3x10 mL). The
combined organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated in vacuo to obtain 25 The amine (167 mg, 0.76 mmol) was
dissolved in MeOH (5 mL) and a solution of (2R,3R)-tartaric acid (114 mg,
0.76 mmol) in methanol was added. The resulting suspension was filtered
off to obtain 25 as its (2R,3R)-tartrate salt (0.27 g). An analytical
sample was obtained by crystallization from MeOH. Yellow oil, yield (0.17
g, 96%). mp: 155-156 °C. IR (KBr), ν : 3425, 3318, 2925, 2866, 1749,
1624, 1600, 1517, 1465, 1445, 1406, 1345, 1321, 1290, 1262, 1229, 1132,
1118, 1110, 1078, 1028, 1006, 989, 940, 901, 684, 611, 567, 524 cm-1.
1H-RMN (400 MHz, CD3OD) δ : 1.09 [s, 6 H, CH3-3(7)], 1.29 [s, 6 H,
(CH3)2-9], 1.39 [dt, J= 11.2 Hz, J' = 3.0 Hz, 2 H, 4(6)-Hendo], 1.77 (t,
J= 3.0 Hz, 1 H, 5-H), 1.85 [dd, J= 11.2 Hz, J' = 1.2 Hz, 2 H, 4(6)-Hexo],
1.93 [dd, J= 10.4 Hz, J' = 2.0 Hz, 2(8)-Hendo], 2.09 [dd, J= 13.2 Hz, J'
= 2.4 Hz, 2(8)-Hexo], 2.85 [s, 6 H, N-(CH3)2], 4.40 [s, 2 H, CH(OH)CO2H].
13C-RMN (100.6 MHz, CD3OD) δ : 21.7 [CH3, CH3-C3(7)], 24.1 [CH3,
(CH3)2-C9], 40.1 [C, C3(7)], 43.2 [CH3, N-(CH3)2], 44.9 (C, C9), 46.3
[CH2, C4(6)], 48.2 [CH2, C2(8)], 50.9 (CH, C5), 74.1 [CH, CH(OH)CO2H],
76.0 (C, C1), 176.8 (C, C=O). MS (EI), m/e (%); significant ions: 221
(M·+, 9), 206 (12), 138 (13), 137 (100), 122 (12). Elemental
analysis:calculated for C19H33NO6: C 61.43%, H 8.95%, N 3.77%. Calculated
for C19H33NO6·0.5H2O: C 59.98%, H 9.01%, N 3.68%; found: C 60.28%, H
8.85%, N 3.43%.
