$DATUM (R)-N,N-Dimethylamino-3-methylbutanoic acid ((R)-55).15 D-Valine ((R)-54)
(10.00 g, 85.41 mmol) was dissolved in H2O (450 mL) and formaldehyde (37%
w/w, 13.9 mL, 171 mmol) and 10% Pd-C (10.0 g) were added. The mixture was
hydrogenated (1 atm) at room temperature (5 d), and then heated to reflux
(10 min). The mixture was filtered through a bed of Celite® (3x) and the
filtrate was evaporated in vacuo. The crude solid was dissolved in a 7:1
mixture of EtOH/H2O, evaporated in vacuo (5x), and then recrystallized
from hot EtOH/acetone to give the desired product. (11.89 g, 96%) as a
white solid: mp 187-188 ºC (lit.16 (S): mp 154 ºC); [α]28 D -33.6° (c
2.1, EtOH); (lit.16 (S): [α]16 D +40.1° (c 2.02, EtOH)); IR (nujol mull)
2947 (br), 1726, 1459, 1373, 1196, 994, 884, 737 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
DMSO-d 6) δ 0.96 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, CH(CH3 )CH3), 1.08 (d, J = 6.8 Hz,
CH(CH3)CH3 ), 2.31-2.42 (m, CH(CH3)2), 2.80 (s, N(CH3 )2), 3.91 (d, J =
4.8 Hz, CH); 13C NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 17.5 (CH(CH3)CH3), 20.7
(CH(CH3)CH3), 26.6 (CH(CH3)2), 41.7 (N(CH3)2), 71.9 (CH), 168.7 (C(O));
LRMS (ESI) 146.11 [M + H+] (calcd for C7H15NO2H+ 146.11).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
