$DATUM N-Methyl-N-benzyl-p-nitrophenethylamine Hydrochloride (15a): A 36%
formaldehyde (11 mL, 0.16 mol) amount was added to compound 14a (10 g,
0.034 mol) in formic acid 88% (6.4 mL, 0.21 mol), it was heated and
refluxed for 4 h, and then, it was adjusted to a solution of pH 14 with
20% NaOH, extracted with acetate, and condensed. Flash chromatography
with acetate-petroleum ether (2:1, v/v) was performed.
N-Methyl-N-benzyl-p-nitrophenethylamine Hydrochloride (15a), yield 9.5 g,
92.3%. mp 218-220 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3 + DMSO-d6) δ 2.75 (s, 3H), 3.15 (s,
4H), 4.20 (s, 2H), 7.45-7.78 (m, 7H), 8.15 (d, 2H).
