$DATUM (1R,5S)-3-Methyl-7-(pyridin-3-yl)-3-azabicyclo[3.3.1]non-6-ene ((+)-5)
(TC-8817). Thiolized silica gel (62.8 g) was added to a 23.1% (w/w)
solution of (+)-15 in isopropanol (2.60 kg of solution, 0.60 kg, 2.99
mol). This treatment was done as a precautionary measure to further
reduce the level of palladium. The suspension was heated to 42 °C for 2
h, cooled, and then stirred at 22 °C for 14 h. The solids were filtered
through a pressure filter fitted with Whatman grade 1 filter paper,
washing the filter cake with isopropanol (0.35 L). The filtrate was
concentrated under reduced pressure (180 mbar) at 45 °C until about 50%
of the solvent was removed. The isopropanol was then solvent swapped with
three separate charges of heptane (3 x 3 L), with vacuum distillation at
161-169 mbar to remove 50% of the solvent following each heptane charge.
The flask contents were then vacuum distilled to dryness at 52 mbar,
leaving 0.588 kg of material in the flask. Formaldehyde (1.636 kg of 37%
aqueous solution, 0.61 kg, 20.2 mol) and formic acid (1.835 kg, 39.9 mol)
were added, and the solution was stirred and heated at reflux (85-87 °C)
for 2 h and then cooled to 41 °C. An IPC by HPLC indicated less than 0.5%
of (+)-15 remaining. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature.
Isopropyl acetate (3 L) was added followed by 10 M NaOH solution (4.46
kg), keeping the internal temperature less than 40 °C. Additional 10 M
NaOH solution (1.0 kg) was added to bring the pH to 13. The phases were
separated, and the lower aqueous phase was extracted with isopropyl
acetate (0.87 L). The combined isopropyl acetate extracts were washed
with 2 M NaOH solution (1.60 kg), followed by a water wash (1.5 L). The
isopropyl acetate phase was separated and dried over MgSO4 (0.63 kg).
After stirring for 30 min, the solids were filtered through a pressure
filter fitted with Whatman grade 1 filter paper, washing the filter cake
with isopropyl acetate (0.6 L). The concentration of (+)-5 in this
isopropyl acetate solution (4.109 kg) was determined to be 14.04% (w/w).
The palladium content was less than 10 ppm in the solid as determined by
ICP-OES. Analytical data were obtained on a sample of the monofumarate
salt. Product (+)-5, yield 0.577 kg, 90%, and the purity by HPLC was
99.0%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD) δ (br s, 1H), 8.46 (br s, 1H) 7.95 (d, J =
7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.43 (br s, 1H), 6.60 (s, 2H), 6.43 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 1H),
3.55 (d, J = 12.5 Hz, 1H), 3.46 (d, J = 12 Hz, 1H), 3.22 (dd, J = 3 Hz,
12.5 Hz, 1H), 3.17 (dd, J = 3.6 Hz, 12.1 Hz, 1H), 2.94 (dd, J = 12.5 Hz,
19.5 Hz, 1H), 2.89 (br s, 1H), 2.81 (s, 3H), 2.67 (d, J = 19.4 Hz, 1H),
2.57 (br s, 1H), 1.97-1.89 (m, 2H). HRMS (ES) m/z Calcd for C14H18N2 + H:
215.1548. Found: 215.1544. [α]20D = +22.27 (c = 1.0, MeOH, HCl salt).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, Eschweiler-Clarke Reaction, kilogram
scale, thiolized silica gel used in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Development of a Scalable Synthesis of a Pyridinyl-3-azabicyclononene, a
Novel Nicotinic Partial Agonist
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Breining, Scott R.; Genus, John F.; Mitchener, J. Pike; Cuthbertson,
Timothy J.; Heemstra, Ronald; Melvin, Matt S.; Dull, Gary M.; Yohannes,
Daniel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2013), 17(3), 413-421

