$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl [Methyl-(1-methyl-2-oxo-2-phenylethyl)amino]acetate Hydrochloride
(6). The HCl salt 5 (6.8 g; 25 mmol) was transformed into the
corresponding base (oil) and its solution in dry acetonitrile (400 mL)
and acetic acid (95 mL) was cooled to 0 °C. Into the stirred solution,
sodium cyanoborohydride (6.1 g; 96 mmol) and 36% aq formaldehyde solution
(140 mL; 1.66 mol) was added. The mixture was stirred at 0 °C, progress
of the methylation could be followed by TLC (hexanes-EtOAc 1:1 after
treating the sheet with NH3 vapor; R f 6>R f 5). The reaction was
complete after 30-40 min. The mixture was diluted with water (500 mL),
its pH was adjusted to neutral with Na2CO3 solution and extracted with
chloroform (3 x 300 mL). The combined organic phase was dried (Na2SO4)
and evaporated. The residue was dissolved in ethanol-diethyl ether 1:5
(50 mL), and acidified with 2N HCl/ dioxane (pH 2). white crystals of
target compound 6 (6.35 g; 89%). Mp 155-157 °C (acetone). IR (KBr): 1680
(C= O ketone); 1738 (C=O ester); 3400 cm-1 (+NH2). 1H NMR (400 MHz;
DMSO-d 6): 1.25 (3H; t; CH2CH 3); 1.50 (3H; d; J = 6.8 Hz; CH 3CHN) 2.89
(3H; s NCH3); 4.08+4.11 (2 x 1H; 2 x d; J gem = 16.8 Hz; +NCH2CO); 4.22
(2H; q; OCH2); 5.35 (1H; q; J = 6.8 Hz; CH3CHN); 7.59 (2H; t; H3'+H5');
7.70 (1H; t; H4'); 8.03 (2H; d; H2'+H6'); 10.20 (1H; brs; +NH). Anal.
(C14H20ClNO3) C, H, N, Cl.
