$DATUM Synthesis of 8-Benzhydryl-4-methyl-1,4-diazabicyclo-[3.3.1]nonane (9).:
8-Benzhydryl-1,4-diazabicyclo[3.3.1]nonane7 (0.05 g, 0.19 mmol) was
refluxed with formaldehyde (1.0 g, 37%/H2O) and formic acid (2.0 g,
88%/H2O) for 3 h, and the excess reagent was removed under reduced
pressure. The residue was partitioned between saturated solution of
NaHCO3 and ethyl acetate. The organic layer was collected, and the water
layer was extracted with ethyl acetate (3x). The crude product was
purified by flash chromatography (EtOAc/MeOH/Et3N = 7/7/0.5) to give 9,
as a colorless oil, yield 0.05 g (87%). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ
1.23-1.40 (2H, m, H-7), 1.45-1.62 (1H, m, H-6ax), 2.18-2.28 (1H, m,
H-6eq), 2.41 (3H, s, CH3), 2.45-2.52 (1H, bm, H-5), 2.60 (1H, m,
NCH2CH2N), 2.77-2.88 (1H, m, NCH2CH2N), 2.90-3.01 (1H, m, NCH2CH2N), 3.03
(1H, bd, J = 12.8 Hz, H-9ax), 3.08-3.17 (1H, m, NCH2CH2N), 3.29 (1H, bd,
J = 13.6 Hz, H-9eq), 3,78 (1H, dt, J = 4.8 Hz, J = 11.2 Hz, CHCH(Ph)2),
3.88 (1H, d, J = 11.2 Hz, CH(Ph)2), 7.11-7.17 (2H, m, ArH), 7.19-7.30
(6H, m, ArH), 7.36 (2H, d, J = 8 Hz, ArH). mp 258-262 °C. Anal.
[C21H26N2•2HCl•1.3H2O] C, H, N.
