$DATUM trans-4-(Dimethylamino)-1-(4-methylbenzenesulfonyl)-1,3,4,5-tetrahydrobenz[cd]indol-5-ol
(49).25 A solution of 17 (3.97 g, 11.59 mmol) in absolute ethanol (150
mL), aqueous formaldehyde (38% w/v; 9.2 mL) and glacial acetic acid (92
mL) was hydrogenated at 30 psi over 10% palladium on carbon (1.56 g) for
65 h. The catalyst was removed by filtration and washed with absolute
ethanol, and the filtrate was evaporated. The residue was dissolved in
dichloromethane (40 mL) and washed with 10% aqueous NaHCO3 (100 mL). The
aqueous layer was extracted with dichloromethane (2 x 120 mL), and the
combined organic phases were dried (Na2SO4) and evaporated. Flash
chromatography of the residue (silica gel, CH2- Cl2-EtOH-NH3(aq) 85:15:0
to 70:9:1) gave 49 together with 400 mg of the corresponding cis isomer.
The oxalate salt was prepared from ethanol-diethyl ether. Yield 3.68 g
(86%). mp 123-126 °C; 1H NMR (360 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 2.32 (3H, s), 2.78 (6H,
s), 2.96-3.12 (1H, m), 3.16-3.26 (1H, m), 3.38-3.54 (1H, m), 5.14 (1H, d,
J = 9.3 Hz), 7.30 (1H, d, J = 7.4 Hz), 7.36- 7.44 (3H, m), 7.55 (1H, s),
7.76 (1H, d, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.86 (2H, d, J = 8.4 Hz); MS (EI) 371 m/z [M +
H]+. Anal. [C20H22N2O3S• C2H2O4] C, H, N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM product further converted into oxalate salt
