$DATUM N-[2-(Benzyloxy)-4-bromo-6-(dimethylamino)phenyl]acetamide (21). Under
stirring, the reaction vessel was charged with starting material 20 (19.5
kg, 58 mol) and methanol (200 l) resulting in an off-white suspension.
While adding formaldehyde (37 % aqueous solution; 45.6 l, 580 mol) at
room temperature a slight increase in temperature (~3 °C) was observed.
Acetic acid (99 %, 19.5 l) was added followed by addition of sodium
cyanoborohydride (6.15 kg, 96.3 mol) in 0.5 kg portions over 2 h.
Throughout the course of addition, gas evolution and a temperature rise
to 30 °C occurred. The temperature was adjusted to 20-25 °C and stirring
continued for further 2 h. The reaction was cooled to 15-20 °C and water
(95 l) was added, followed by addition of aqueous sodium hydroxide
solution (24 l) resulting in a pH value of 7-8. During these additions
again a temperature rise to 24 °C / 28 °C, respectively, could be
observed. The mixture was stirred overnight, the solvent was distilled
off (170 l) and the suspension cooled to 12-17 °C. The formed product was
filtrated off, transferred back to the reactor and dissolved in ethyl
acetate (235 l). From the brown solution, solvent was distilled off in
vacuo until a residual volume of 100 l was obtained. Again, the
suspension was filtrated and the filter cake dried at 60 °C in vacuo
furnishing the title compound 21 as off-white crystals (17.2 kg, 84 %
yield, HPLC purity >99 %):. m.p. 177 °C. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 200 MHz): δ =
1.97 (bs, 3 H), 2.68 (s, 6 H), 5.07 (s, 2 H), 6.73 (d, 1 H), 6.87 (bs, 1
H), 7.36 (mc, 5 H), 8.92 (bs, 1 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM scalable, exothermic reaction stage 3, portionwise addn. of sodium
cyanoborohydride
