$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N2-Benzyloxycarbonyl-(S)-2-amino-3(dimethylamino)propanoic Acid
(Z-A2pr(Me2)-OH).- To a vigorously stirred suspension of Z-A2Pr-OH
(2.22g, 9.3 mmol) in acetonitrile (30 mL), 30% formaldehyde (4.2 mL) and
NaBH3CN (1.03 g, 16 mmol) were added. After 15 min, acetic acid was added
until the pH was neutral and stirring was continued for 24 h. After
evaporation of solvents, the residue was dissolved in methanol (50 mL)
and SOCl2 (0.2 mL) was added dropwise and the mixture was left standing
for 12 h with occasional stirring. After evaporation of methanol, the
residue was dissolved in water (5 mL), neutralized with 1 M aqueous
NaHCO3 and extracted with chloroform (2x 20 mL). The organic layer was
evaporated, the oily residue dissolved in stoichiometric amount of IM
NaOH (8.3 mL) and methanol (10 mL) and kept for 2 h at room temperature.
The concentrated solution was adsorbed on AG 1X2 column (OH, 0.8 x 10
cm). Elution with 1 M acetic acid and evaporation of eluate to dryness
gave the solid residue which was crystallized from methanol-ethyl ether.
1.98 g (80%) of the title compound. mp.138-139°(dec.). TLC: Rf: A-0.19,
Rf: B-0.31 [α]20 D = -18.2° (c = 1, H2O) 1H NMR (D2O,200 MHz): δ 2.75
(N(CH3)2, s,6H), 3.18 (CHAHB,dd,1H, JAB = 13.2 Hz, JAX = 8,6 Hz), 3.35
(CHAHB, dd, 1H, JAX = 6.2 Hz, JAB = 13.2 Hz), 4.20 (CH, dd, 1H, JAX = 6.2
Hz, JBX = 8.6 Hz), 4.98 (PhCH2, s, 2H), 7.27 (C6H5, m, 5H). 13C NMR (D2O,
200 MHz): δ 46.02 (CH2)1 53.98 (CH), 61.56 (N(CH3)2), 70.28 (PhCH2),
130.79, 131.39,131.70 (CH arom), 139.01 (CHarom)1160.75 (COureth)1177.18
(COOH) Anal. Calcd for C13H18N2O4: C158.63; H, 6.81; N, 10.52. Found: C,
58.82; H17.03; N, 10.28.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A facile synthesis of
N2-benzyloxycarbonyl-(S)-2-amino-3-(dimethylamino)propanoic acid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Andruszkiewicz, Ryszard; Walkowiak, Aleksandra
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Preparations and Procedures International (2001), 33(4), 379-381

