$DATUM N,N-Dimethyl-2-(1-benzenesulfonyl-5-methoxy-2-methyl-1H-indol-3-yl)ethylamine
(41). To a stirred solution of
2-(5-methoxy-2-methyl-1H-indol-3-yl)ethylamine hydrochloride34 (1.6 g,
6.55 mmol) in methanol (100 mL) was added a 30% (w/v) solution of sodium
methoxide in methanol (1.24 mL, 6.55 mmol), then acetic acid (1.50 mL,
26.2 mmol), followed by sodium cyanoborohydride (0.82 g, 13.1 mmol). A
38% (w/v) aqueous solution of formaldehyde (1.24 mL, 15.7 mmol) in
methanol (30 mL) was then added dropwise over 40 min, and the mixture was
stirred overnight. Aqueous NaOH (4 N, 50 mL) was then added, the methanol
was evaporated, and the aqueous residue was extracted with ethyl acetate.
The organic extract was washed with brine (50 mL), dried (Na2SO4), and
evaporated to give 41. The oxalate salt was prepared in ethanol-diethyl
ether. Yield 1.215 g (80%). mp 212-215 °C; 1H NMR (360 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ
2.32 (3H, s), 2.82 (6H, s), 2.95 (2H, m), 3.09 (2H, m), 3.76 (3H, s),
6.64 (1H, dd, J = 8.7, 2.3 Hz), 6.99 (1H, d, J = 2.3 Hz), 7.13 (1H, d, J
= 8.7 Hz); MS (ES+) m/z 233 [M + H]+. Anal. [C14H20N2O•C2H2O4] C, H, N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM product further converted into oxalate salt
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Arylsulfonylindole derivatives as serotonin 5-HT6 receptor ligands
