$DATUM 3-((3S,7R,8R,9αR)-2,7,8-Trimethyl-3-phenyl-octahydro-1Hpyrido[
1,2-α]pyrazin-8-yl)phenol (7). To a solution of 5 (0.1 g, 0.30 mmol) in
tetrahydrofuran (5 mL) and ethanol (5 mL) was added triethylamine (0.067
g, 0.66 mmol) and formaldehyde (40% aqueous solution; 0.05 mL, 0.60
mmol). After 10 min, sodium cyanoborohydride (0.03 g, 0.36 mmol) was
added to the mixture, which was stirred at room temperature for 60 h. The
mixture was concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude product was
purified by column chromatography (eluent: dichloromethane/
methanol/ammonium hydroxide mixtures of increasing polarity). Yield 76%
(white solid); white solid;1H NMR (CD3OD) δ 0.77 (d, J = 7 Hz, 3H), 1.37
(s, 3H), 1.57 (d, J = 13 Hz, 1H), 1.96 (t, J = 13 Hz, 1H), 2.07 (s, 4H),
2.24 (t, J = 11 Hz, 1H), 2.32 (t, J = 11 Hz, 1H), 2.55 (m, 1H), 2.66 (m,
2H), 2.74 (m, 1H), 2.92 (d, J = 10 Hz, 1H), 3.24 (d, J = 9 Hz, 1H), 6.58
(dd, J = 8 and 2 Hz, 1H), 6.72 (t, J = 2 Hz, 1H), 6.76 (d, J = 8 Hz, 1H),
7.11 (t, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 7.29 (m, 1H), 7.36 (m, 4H); LCMS (ESI) m/z 351 (M
+ H+). Anal. (C23H30N2O.0.4H2O) C, H, N.
