$DATUM Ethyl 1-alkyl-4-phenyl-1,2,5,6-tetrahydropyridine-3-carboxylate 41. A
mixture of 14 (2 g, 8.65 mmol), NaCNBH3 (1.63 g, 25.95 mmol), aldehyde
(paraformaldehyde, propionaldehyde, or butyraldehyde), and EtOH (20 mL)
was stirred at room temperature overnight followed by standard aqueous
workup. The crude product was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (2:1 hexanes:EtOAc) to afford 41. Ethyl
1-methyl-4-phenyl-1,2,5,6-tetrahydropyridine-3-carboxylate 41a. Colorless
oil, 1.59 g, 75% yield 1H NMR (300 MHz): δ 7.26-7.38 (m, 3H), 7.14 (dd, J
= 7.5, 1.5 Hz, 2H), 3.89 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 3.33 (t, J = 2.7 Hz, 2H),
2.66 (m, 2H), 2.59 (m, 2H), 2.47 (s, 3H), 0.86 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H) ppm;
13C NMR (75 MHz): δ 167.1, 146.4, 142.3, 128.1, 127.3, 126.9, 125.3,
60.3, 55.3, 51.9, 45.6, 34.1, 13.8 ppm; EI-MS m/z 245 (M+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM paraformaldehyde used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
