$DATUM A mixture of paraformaldehyde (0.016 g, 0.053 mmol) in MeOH (10 mL) and
AcOH (1 mL) was heated at reflux overnight. The reaction mixture was
cooled to ambient temperature and
4-methyl-6-(3-methyl-azetidin-3-ylamino)-7-phenyl-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenan
thren-3-one trifluoroacetic acid (intermediate obtained at Step D during
preparation of compound 22, 0.020 g, 0.053 mmol) was added. The reaction
mixture was stirred for 2 h. Sodium cyanoborohydride (0.013 g, 0.212
mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred overnight at room
temperature. The solvent was removed in vacuo and the residue was
purified by preparative HPLC (Table 2, Method 3). HPLC: Column: YMC-Actus
Triart C18 150×30 mm, 5 µum. Mobile phase: MeCN in water (0.075% TFA),
from 27% to 47% in 11 min; Flowrate: 25 mL/min. Wavelength: 220 nm.
6-[(1,3-dimethyl-azetidin-3-yl)-methyl-amino]-4-methyl-7-phenyl-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one
trifluoroacetic acid (0.015 g, 0.036 mmol, 68%) as a white solid. 1H NMR
(CD3OD, 400 MHz): δ 7.51 (m, 4H), 7.40 (m, 1H), 7.06 (m , 2H), 4.64 (m,
2H), 3.84 (m, 4H), 2.76 (s, 3H), 2.35 (s, 3H), 1.49 (m, 6H). LC/MS (Table
1, Method 4) Rt = 1.689 min.; MS m/z: 406 [M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM paraformaldehyde used (stage 1)
