$DATUM N,N-dimethyl-(2-isopropyladamant-1-yl)amine (2R, 3R)-tartrate,
19d·(2R,3R)-tartrate. A mixture of 11·HCl (0.23 g, 1 mmol), NaBH3CN (0.18
g, 2.9 mmol), formaldehyde (0.25 mL, 37% aq. solution, 3.0 mmol), acetic
acid (0.15 mL) in MeOH (5 mL) with a CaCl2 tube was stirred at room
temperature for 8 h. More NaBH3CN (0.18 g, 2.9 mmol) and formaldehyde
(0.25 mL, 37% aq. solution, 3.0 mmol) were added and the reaction was
stirred at room temperature overnight. The reaction was concentrated
under vacuo. The residue was dissolved in H2O (10 mL) and the aqueous
layer was basified with an aqueous solution of NaOH 10 N (3 mL). The
aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (4x10 mL). The combined organic
extracts were dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo to
obtain the desired amine 19d. An analytical sample of the
(2R,3R)-tartrate of 19d was obtained by adding (2R,3R)-tartaric acid (60
mg, 0.40 mmol) to a solution of 19d (89 mg, 0.40 mmol) in MeOH (5 mL).
Pale orange oil, yield (0.15 g, 68%). mp: 63-64 °C (MeOH). IR (KBr), ν :
3336, 3057, 2919, 2906, 2732, 2531, 1735, 1676, 1467, 1451, 1420, 1354,
1306, 1264, 1213, 1141, 1111, 1086, 997, 900, 842, 790, 679, 604, 481
cm-1. 1H-RMN (400 MHz, CD3OD) δ : 1.10 (d, J= 6.4 Hz, 3 H) and 1.14 (d,
J= 6.8 Hz, 3 H) (CH3CHCH3), 1.57 (d, J= 13.2 Hz, 1 H, 2-H), 1.68-1.84
(complex signal, 4 H, 4-Hendo + 6-H2 + 10-Hendo), 1.91-1.94 (complex
signal, 2 H, 8-Hendo + 9-Hendo), 2.01-2.14 (complex signal, 5 H, CH3CHCH3
+ 4-Hexo + 8-Hexo + 9-Hexo + 10-Hexo), 2.23-2.26 (complex signal, 2 H,
5-H + 7-H), 2.32 (bs, 1 H, 3-H), 2.82 [s, 6 H, N-(CH3)2], 4.41 [s, 2 H,
CH(OH)CO2H]. 13C-RMN (100.6 MHz, CD3OD) δ : 1.6 (CH3) and 25.0 (CH3)
(CH3CHCH3), 27.1 (CH, CH3CHCH3), 30.7 (CH, C3), 31.1 (CH) and 31.5 (CH)
(C5 and C7), 32.4 [CH2 C4(10)], 34.6 (CH2 and 37. 4 (CH2 (C8 and C9),
36.2 (CH2 C6), 37.7 [CH3, N-(CH3)2], 40.0 (CH, C2), 68.1 (C, C1), 74.1
[CH, CH(OH)CO2H], 176.6 (C, C=O). MS (EI), m/e (%); significant ions: 222
(9), 221 (M·+, 50), 178 (23), 164 (21), 136 (15), 123 (35), 122 (100),
121 (14), 91 (10), 85 (37), 79 (11). Elemental analysis: calculated for
C19H33NO6: C 61.43%, H 8.95%, N 3.77%; calculated for C19H33NO6·1 H2 : C
58.59%, H 9.06%, N 3.60%; found: C 58.32%, H 8.85%, N 3.40%.
