$DATUM 6-Methyl-4, 5,6, 7-tetrahydrofuro[2,3-c]pyridine (25). To the solution of
24 (1.05 g, 4.70 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2 mL) was added MeOH solution saturated
with HCl (30 mL). After stirred for 2 h at room temperature, the mixture
was concen- trated. To the suspension of the residue in CH2Cl2 (20 mL)
was added Et3N (1.31 mL, 9.40 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 15 min
at room temperature. To the mixture were added AcOH (810 μL, 14.1 mmol),
37% aq HCHO (610 μL, 7.11 mmol), and sodium triacetoxy borohydride (1.51
g, 7.12 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred for 1 h at room
temperature under an argon atmosphere and poured into sat. NaHCO3. The
separated organic layer was washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, and
concentrated in vacuo. Purification of the residue by column
chromatography (CH2Cl2/MeOH, 10/1) gave 25 (434 mg, 67%) as a colorless
oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 2.48 (3H, s), 2.56 (2H, t, J = 5.6 Hz), 2.67 (2H,
t, J = 5.6 Hz), 3.48 (2H, s), 6.23 (1H, d, J = 2.0 Hz), 7.25 (1H, s).
