$DATUM trans-3-(3,4,5-Trimethoxyphenyl)acrylic Acid 5-[(5-Hydroxypentyl)
methylamino]pentyl Ester (48). To a solution of 0.8 g (1.95 mmol) of 43
in 25 mL of anhydrous ethanol were added 24 mL of HCOOH and 24 mL of
HCHO. The mixture was heated to 80 °C for 7 h and concentrated in vacuo.
The residue was then dissolved in CH2Cl2 and the organic layer was washed
with a saturated solution of Na2CO3 and with water. After drying with
Na2SO4, the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The crude product
was then purified by flash chromatography using CH2Cl2/abs EtOH/ethyl
ether/ petroleum ether/NH4OH 360:180:360:900:9.9 as the eluting system.
Compound 48 was obtained as an oil (0.53 g, 64% yield). IR (neat): ν cm-1
3404 (OH), 1710 (CO). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.55 (d, J = 16.1 Hz, 1H, CH=CH),
6.72 (s, 2H, aromatics), 6.31 (d, J = 16.1 Hz, 1H, CH=CH), 4.16 (t, J =
6.2 Hz, 2H, CH2O), 3.85 (s, 6H, 2OCH3), 3.83 (s, 3H, OCH3), 3.59 (t, J =
6.1 Hz, 2H, CH2OH), 2.62 (s, 1H, OH), 2.31-2.27 (m, 4H, 2CH2N), 2.16 (s,
3H, NCH3), 1.76-1.22 (m, 12H, 6CH2) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Exploratory Chemistry toward the Identification of a New Class of
Multidrug Resistance Reverters Inspired by Pervilleine and Verapamil
Models
