$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Intermediate 2: 4-N-Methylaminostyrene.2 To a stirred mixture of
4-aminostyrene (0.833 g, 7 mmol) and paraformaldehyde (1.05 g, 35 mmol)
in 20 mL MeOH was added sodium methoxide (1.89 g, 35 mmol). The reaction
mixture was heated to reflux for 2 h and cooled to 0 °C with an ice bath.
Sodium borohydride (1.323 g, 35 mmol) was added in three portions.
Reaction mixture was heated to reflux again for 1 h and cooled back to
r.t.. After standard workup with CH2Cl2, the crude product was purified
by FC (EtOAc/Hexanes, 7/93) to afford the title compound as light yellow
oil (0.539 g, 58%). 1H NMR δ 7.28 (dt, 2H, J = 8.6Hz, J = 2.0 Hz),
6.71-6.54 (m, 3H), 5.54 (dd, 1H, J 1 = 17.5 Hz,J 2 = 1.0 Hz), 5.03 (dd,
1H, J 1 = 10.8 Hz, J 2 = 1.0 Hz), 3.78 (br s, 1H), 2.86 (s, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM paraformaldehyde used
