$DATUM N-Methyl-4-(5-nitro-1H-indol-3-yl)cyclohex-3-enamine ((±)-8). A solution
of compound 6 (1.44 g, 5.62 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (20 mL) was
treated with AcOH (0.31 mL, 5.62 mmol), methylamine hydrochloride (0.37
g, 5.62 mmol), and NaBH(OAC)3 (1.78 g, 8.43 mmol) at rt and stirred
overnight (14 h). Same workup as in (±)-7. The crude was purified by
column chromatography (2 M NH3 in MeOH:CH2Cl2 1:9). Compound (±)-8 (0.82
g, 54%) as a solid. 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6) δ 11.85 (brs, 1H), 8.67 (s, 1H),
8.00 (d, 1H, J = 7.5 Hz), 7.63 (s, 1H), 7.54 (d, 1H, J = 9.0 Hz), 6.13
(brs, 1H), 2.70-2.60 (m, 1H), 2.57-2.40 (m, 3H), 2.35 (s, 3H), 2.01-1.97
(m, 2H), 1.53-1.44 (m, 1H). ESI-MS (m/z, %) 272 (MH+, 100).
