$DATUM (R)-4-methyl-6-[methyl-(1,3-dimethyl-azetidin-3-yl)-amino]-7-trifluoromethyl-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one
trifluoroacetic acid (20). To a mixture of
(R)-4-methyl-6-(3-methyl-azetidin-3-ylamino)-7-trifluoromethyl-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one
trifluoroacetic acid1 (0.120 g, 0.250 mmol) in MeOH (5 mL) and AcOH (0.5
mL) was added paraformaldehyde (neat, 0.060 g, 2 mmol). The reaction
mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 30 min then NaBH3CN (0.126
g, 2 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was heated at 50 °C for 5
h. The reaction mixture was cooled to ambient temperature and the solvent
was removed in vacuo. The residue was purified by preparative HPLC (Table
2, Method 5) and further separated by chiral SFC (Table 3, Method 4).
HPLC: Column: YMC-Actus Triart C18 150×30 mm, 5 µm. Mobile phase: MeCN in
water (0.075% TFA), from 20% to 40% in 11 min; Flowrate: 25 mL/min.
Wavelength: 220 nm.
(R)-4-methyl-6-[methyl-(1,3-dimethyl-azetidin-3-yl)-amino]-7-trifluoromethyl-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one
trifluoroacetic acid (compound 20, 0.020 g, 12%) as a white solid. LC/MS
(Table 1, Method 3) Rt = 1.672 min; MS m/z: 384 [M+H]+. SFC (Table 4,
Method 3) Rt = 5.89 min.
