$DATUM 2-[(2-Dimethylaminoethyl)methylamine]-4-methyl-6-methylaminoquinoline
(4u). A solution of
6-amino-2-(dimethylaminoethyl)methylamine-4-methylquinoline (4c, 1.0 g,
3.9 mmol), sodium methoxide (1.05 g, 19.4 mmol) and paraformaldehyde (174
mg, 5.8 mmol) in dry MeOH (60 mL) was stirred at 40 °C. After 48 h the
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature and added sodium
borohydride (322 mg, 8.51 mmol), and stirring was continued at 50 °C.
After 24 h the reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo and the residue
was partitioned between CH2Cl2 and 1 N NaHCO3. The organic phase was
washed with brine, dried (MgSO4) and concentrated. The residue was
purified by automated flash chromatography (Combiflash, SiO2, CH2Cl2 to
CH2Cl2:MeOH:NH4OH, 90:9:1, gradient over 30 min) to give 100 mg (10%) of
the title compound. 1H NMR (CDCl3): 2.35 (s, 6H), 2.54 (s, 3H), 2.58
(“t”, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H), 2.92 (s, 3H), 3.17 (s, 3H), ~3.70 (br s, 1H), 3.77
(“t”, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H), 6.70 (s, 1H), 6.74 (d, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H), 6.97 (dd,
J = 8.9, 2.6 Hz, 1H), 7.56 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 1H); MS ESI+ m/z 273.2 [M +
H].
