$DATUM 1-Methyl-piperidine-4-carboxylic acid
(3-oxo-2,3,4,10-tetrahydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-6-yl)-amide
(15p). Piperidine-4-carboxylic acid
(3-oxo-2,3,4,10-tetrahydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-6-yl)-amide
hydrochloride acid (compound 15o, 0.030 g, 0.091 mmol) was treated with
paraformaldehyde (10 mg/mL in MeOH, 10 mL, 0.446 mmol) and stirred at
ambient temperature for 1 h. NaBH3CN (0.017 g, 0.273 mmol) was added and
the reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 4 h. The
reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo and the residue was purified
by prep-HPLC (Table 3, Method 3). Method 3: Column: YMC-Actus Triart C18
150x30 mm, 5 μm. Mobile phase: acetonitrile in water (0.05% ammonia
solution), from 19% to 34% in 11 min; Flow rate: 25 mL/min. Wavelength:
220 nm. 1-methyl-piperidine-4-carboxylic acid
(3-oxo-2,3,4,10-tetrahydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triazaphenanthren-6-yl)-amide
(compound 15p, 0.003 g, 9%) as a white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD): δ
7.29 (s, 1H), 7.08 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 6.90 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 4.55
(s, 2H), 4.27 (s, 2H), 3.45 (overlapped, 4H), 2.98-2.95 (m, 3H), 2.29
(m,1H), 2.13 (m, 2H), 1.86 (m, 2H). LC/MS (Table 1, Method 5) Rt = 1.320
min.; MS m/z: 344 [M+H]+.
