$DATUM A solution of formaldehyde (37% w/w in water) (3.59 mL, 48.3 mmol) in
MeOH (20 mL) was added dropwise to a stirred solution of
6-(piperidin-4-ylsulfonyl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-amine dihydrochloride (7.45
g, 20.1 mmol) and sodium cyanoborohydride (2.53 g, 40.2 mmol) in MeOH
(300 mL) at rt over a period of 5 min under nitrogen. The reaction
mixture was stirred for 1 h and then neutralized with saturated NaHCO3
(150 mL). Approximately 200 mL of the MeOH was removed under reduced
pressure and the resulting suspension was extracted with DCM (3 x 200
mL). The combined organic layers were washed with brine (100 mL) then
evaporated. Crude
6-(1-methylpiperidin-4-ylsulfonyl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-amine which was used
without further purification.. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) 1.44-1.55 (2H,
m), 1.74-1.84 (4H, m), 2.10 (3H, s), 2.77-2.82 (2H, m), 3.03-3.11 (1H,
m), 7.46 (1H, d), 7.59-7.62 (1H, m), 8.00 (2H, s), 8.15 (1H, d); m/z MH+
= 312.
