$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N,N-(diMe)-Aib-OBzl. TFA, N(Me)-Aib-OBzl (1.47 g, 4.6 mmol) was dissolved
in water (1.2 mL). Then, formic acid (868 μL, 23 mmol) and 37%
formaldehyde (1.21 mL, 16.1 mmol) were successively added, and the
mixture was placed under reflux. After 24 h, the mixture was diluted in
ether (5 mL) and water (5 mL). The aqueous layer was neutralized at pH 7.
Then the residue was dissolved in ethyl acetate (10 mL) and washed with
saturated aqueous sodium chloride (20 mL). The organic layer was dried
over sodium sulfate and filtered, and the solvent was removed in vacuo to
afford N,N-(diMe)- Aib-OBzl as an oil. N,N-(diMe)-Aib-OBzl Rf = 0.41
(ethyl acetate/pyridine/acetic acid/ water, 40:20:5:10). 1H NMR (200 MHz,
CDCl3): δ(s, 6H, Aib), 2.31 and 2.32 (2s, 6H, 2Me), 5.21 (s, 2H, CH2
(Bzl)), 7.39 (m, 5H, Bzl). MS (ES), m/z: 222.34 [M + H]+.
