$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
7-(2H-benzo[e][1,3]oxazin-3(4H)-yl)-2-phenylchroman-4-one derivatives.
Step 1: Synthesis of substituted Schiff bases 7-Aminoflavone (0.001 mol)
was transferred into a 50 ml round bottom flask. Salicylaldehyde (0.001
mol) was added dropwise. Mixture was kept in the microwave oven and
irradiated for 10 min at 450 watt. Completion of the reaction was checked
by monitoring the TLC pattern. TLC was carried out on coated alumina
plate (n-hexane and ethyl acetate, 6:4) and visualized under short wave
UV light. Schiff's base, obtained, was washed 3-4 times, with small
quantities of cold ethanol, filtered, dried, and recrystallized from
chloroform and pet. ether (1:1) to afford light orange microcrystalline
powder. Step 2: Reduction of Schiff bases Schiff's base (0.001 mol) was
dissolved in methanol (20 ml) by gentle warming. Sodium borohydride (0.02
mol) was added and stirred for 1 h, and heated to 400°C for 10-15 min.
Completion of the reaction was checked by monitoring using the TLC
pattern. TLC was carried out on coated alumina plate (n-hexane and ethyl
acetate, 6:4) and visualized under short wave UV light. Methanol was
evaporated under reduced pressure. The residue was washed with water,
dried, and recrystallized from chloroform and pet. ether (1:1) to afford
pale yellow microcrystalline powder. Step 3: Formation of 1,3-benzoxazine
ring Reduced Schiff's base (0.001 mol) was transferred into a 50 ml round
bottom flask. Chloroform (20 ml) was added and mixture was heated on an
electric hot plate with constant stirring till complete dissolution was
achieved, and then formalin 37 % (1 ml) was added dropwise. Mixture was
refluxed for 32 h for cyclization into benzoxazine. Completion of the
reaction was checked by monitoring, using the TLC pattern. TLC was
carried out on coated alumina plate (n-hexane and ethyl acetate, 6:4) and
visualized under UV light. Chloroform was distilled off under reduced
pressure. The residue obtained was recrystallized from chloroform and
pet. ether (1:1), and the benzoxazine was obtained as light yellow
microcrystalline powders.
7-(6,8-Dimethyl-2H-benzo[e][1,3]oxazin-3(4H)-yl)-2-phenyl-4H-chromen-4-one
(6g) Light yellow solid. m.p. 161-162°C. MS, m/z: 383.15 (100.0 %),
384.16 (27.4 %), 385.16 (4.2 %), (C25H21NO3, calc. 383.44). FT-IR (KBr)
(cm-1): 3332.43 (N-H), 1255 (C-O str of ether), 1602.34 (C═N str),
1587.13 (Ring C═C str), 2961.4 (C-H str of CH3), 3047.3 (C-H str for
aromatic ring). 1H NMR (300 MHz) CDCl3, δ (ppm): 7.4-7.5 (5H, m), 6.56
(2H, d), 6.71 (1H, s), 6.31 (1H, s), 6.82 (1H, s), 7.7 (1H, d), 5.4 (2H,
s), 4.7 (2H, s), 2.35 (6H, s). 13C NMR (100 MHz) CDCl3, δ (ppm): 163.4,
104.5, 182.0, 113.2, 131.1, 109.1, 156.1, 100.4, 158.1, 130.1, 126.3,
128.5, 128.1, 128.5, 126.1, 90.8, 57.5, 122.0, 153.7, 124.2, 130.2,
130.4, 127.8, 15.0, 24.9. Anal. Calcd. C, 78.31; H, 5.52; N, 3.65; O,
12.52. Found: C, 78.30; H, 5.50; N, 3.67; O, 12.55.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (in stage 1), 450 W used in stage 1
