Hydrochloride (15a): A 36% formaldehyde (11 mL, 0.16 mol) amount was
added to compound 14a (10 g, 0.034 mol) in formic acid 88% (6.4 mL, 0.21
mol), it was heated and refluxed for 4 h, and then, it was adjusted to a
solution of pH 14 with 20% NaOH, extracted with acetate, and condensed.
Flash chromatography with acetate-petroleum ether (2:1, v/v) was
performed. N-Methyl-N-(p-methylbenzyl)-p-nitrophenethylamineHydrochloride
(15b). mp 185-186.5 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3 + DMSO-d6): δ 2.30 (s, 3H), 2.65
(s, 3H), 3.35 (s, 4H), 4.40 (q, 2H), 7.20-7.60 (m, 6H), 8.12 (d, 2H).
