$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
6-(2H-1,3-benzoxazin-3(4H)-yl)-2-phenyl-4H-chromen-4-one derivatives.
Step 1: Preparation of 6-{[(1E)-(2-hydroxyphenyl) methylidene]
amino}-2-phenyl-4H-chromen-4-one (1) 6-Aminoflavone (0.001 mol) was
dissolved in 20 ml ethanol and transferred into round bottom flask. The
mixture was heated on water bath till complete dissolution was achieved.
To the resulting mixture, salicylaldehyde (0.001 mol) was added dropwise,
and mixture was refluxed for 4 h. The mixture was cooled; Schiff's base
(1) was separated, filtered, dried and recrystallized from chloroform and
pet. ether (1:1) to afford orange microcrystalline powder. Step 2:
Preparation of 6-[(2-hydroxybenzyl) amino]-2-phenyl-4H-chromen-4-one (2)
Compound 1 (0.001 mol) was dissolved in methanol (20 ml) by gentle
warming. Sodium borohydride (0.02 mol) was added and mixture was stirred
for 1 h. The mixture was heated to 40 °C for 10-15 min. Methanol was
evaporated under reduced pressure. The residue was washed with water,
dried, and recrystallized from chloroform and pet. ether (1:1) to afford
pale yellow microcrystalline powder of compound 2. Step 3: Preparation of
6-(2H-1,3-benzoxazin-3(4H)-yl)-2-phenyl-4H-chromen-4-one (3) The compound
2 (0.001 mol) and formalin (37 %, 1 ml) were refluxed on a water bath for
12-14 h, in chloroform (15 ml), for cyclization into benzoxazine.
Chloroform was distilled off under reduced pressure. The residue obtained
was recrystallized from chloroform and pet. ether (1:1), and the
benzoxazines were obtained as light yellow microcrystalline powders.
6-(6,8-Dibromo-2H-1,3-benzoxazin-3(4H)-yl)-2-phenyl-4H-chromen-4-one (3c)
Light yellow solid. m.p. 191-192°C, m/z: 512.94 (100.0 %), 510.94 (51.4
%), 514.94 (49.3 %) (C23H15NO3Br2, calc. 513.18); FT-IR (KBr) (cm-1):
3332.43 (N-H), 1255 (C-O str of ether), 1602.34 (C═N str), 1587.13 (Ring
C═C str), 2961.4 (C-H str of CH3), 3047.3 (C-H str for aromatic ring). 1H
NMR (300 MHz) CDCl3, δ (ppm): 7.4-7.52 (6H, m), 6.7-6.74 (3H, m), 7.1
(1H, s), 6.9 (1H, s), 5.9 (2H, s), 4.7 (2H, s). 13C NMR (100 MHz) CDCl3,
δ (ppm): 163.7, 104.5, 182.2, 124.9, 113.0, 144.3, 120.8, 118.6, 146.8,
130.4, 126.4, 128.7, 128.0, 128.7, 126.4, 89.8, 55.5, 126.6, 152.6,
132.7, 117.4, 134.1, 114.2. Anal. Calcd. C, 53.83; H, 2.95; Br, 31.14; N,
2.73; O, 9.35. Found: C, 53.81; H, 2.96; Br, 31.12; N, 2.71; O, 9.34.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (in stage 1)
