$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-(1-Benzylpropyl)-1-methyl-3-(4-phenoxyphenyl)urea (40f). To a 100 mL
round-bottomed flask equipped with a magnetic stirring bar were added a
solution of 1-phenyl-2- butanone (1.5 mL, 10 mmol) in EtOH (15 mL),
triethylamine (2.8 mL, 20 mmol), methylamine hydrochloride (1.4 g, 20
mmol), and titanium(IV) isopropoxide (5.9 mL, 20 mmol). After 3 h, NaBH4
(0.60 g, 16 mmol) was added, and the reaction mixture was stirred for an
additional 3 h. Aqueous NH3 was then added, and the white precipitate
that fell out of solution was removed by filtration. Water was added to
the filtrate, and the aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3x). The
combined organic fractions were washed with 10% HCl, the layers were
separated, and the aqueous layer was washed with CH2Cl2. The aqueous
layer was neutralized with 2 N NaOH, and the mixture was extracted with
CH2Cl2 (3x). The combined organic fractions were dried over MgSO4,
filtered, and concentrated in vacuo to give crude
methyl(benzylpropyl)amine as a clear oil (0.80 g crude yield)
1-Methyl-3-(4-phenoxyphenyl)-1-(2-(4-pyridyl)-1-methylethyl) urea
Hydrochloride (40m). Methyl(2-(4-pyridyl)1- methylethyl)amine was
prepared according to the procedure described for the synthesis of
methyl(benzylpropyl)amine (see the procedure for 40f) by using
4-pyridylacetone (1.5 g, 10 mmol), titanium(IV) isopropoxide (5.9 mL, 20
mmol), methylamine hydrochloride (1.4 g, 20 mmol), triethylamine (2.8 mL,
20 mmol), EtOH (15 mL), and sodium borohydride (0.60 g, 16 mmol). The
intermediate amine was isolated upon workup as a yellow oil and was
carried on without purification (1.7 g crude yield) MS m/z: 151 (M + 1).
