$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.10.
(S)-3-(1-(3-(Dimethylamino)propyl)-1-(4-fluorophenyl)-1,3-dihydroisobenzofuran-5-yl)
acrylonitrile) (10): Cyanoacetic acid (0.165 g, 1.9 mmol) and morpholine
(0.169 g, 1.9 mmol) were added to the solution of compound 9 (0.489 g,
1.5 mmol) in DMF (5 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at reflux for 5
h. The solvent was evaporated under vacuum. The product was dissolved in
H2O (20 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (3 × 20 mL). The organic layer was
dried, concentrated and purified by column chromatography using 3% MeOH/
CHCl3 as the eluent to afford material with a mixture of E and Z isomers
(∼1.77:1, as determined by the 1H NMR).
1-(3-(dimethylamino)propyl)-1-(4-fluorophenyl)-1,3-dihydroisobenzofuran-5-carbonitrile
(citalopram). SERT Ki or Kd (nM) [SE interval]: 2.6 [1.8-3.8].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel and High Affinity Fluorescent Ligands for the Serotonin Transporter
Based on (S)-Citalopram
