$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (R)-8-(3,5-Difluorophenyl)-6,8-dimethy6,9-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-10-one. To
a solution of
(R)-8-(3,5-difluorophenyl)-8-methy6,9-diazaspiro[4.5]decan-10-one (2.04
g, 7.26 mmol) and paraformaldehyde (0.654 g, 21.8 mmol) in MeOH (20 mL)
and acetic acid (2.08 mL, 36.3 mmol) was added sodium cyanoborohydride
(0.684 g, 10.9 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at ambient
temperature for 16 h and at 50 °C for 27 h. After 23 h, additional
paraformaldehyde (1.00 g, 33.3 mmol) was added and at 27 h additional
sodium cyanoborohydride (0.684 g, 10.9 mmol) was added. The MeOH was
removed and the crude mixture was partitioned between sat. NaHCO3 (50 mL)
and CH2Cl2 (50 mL). The layers were separated and the aqueous layer was
further extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 X 50 mL). The combined organic layers
were dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo to provide of
the title compound, which was used without further purification. Yellow
foam, yield 2.13 g. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 6.90-6.85 (2H, m); 6.72-6.67 (1H,
m); 5.73 (1H, s); 2.74 (2H, s); 2.19 (3H, s); 2.12- 1.62 (8H, m); 1.58
(3H, s). MS: m/z = 295 (M +1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM paraformaldehyde used, incremental addition of paraformaldehyde and
sodium cyanoborohydride
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM [11C]MK-4232: The First Positron Emission Tomography Tracer for the
Calcitonin Gene-Related Peptide Receptor
