$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: tert-Butyl
(1s,4s)-4-(5-fluoro-2-(4'-hydroxy-2'-(morpholinomethyl)bipheny3-yloxy)nicotinamido)cyclohexylcarbamate
35 [General Method J]. To a solution of 32 (2.00 g, 1 eq) in CH2Cl2 (40
mL) were added morpholine (1.3 mL, 4 eq) and acetic acid (0.21 mL, 1 eq).
The mixture was stirred at rt for 40 min then methanol (10 mL) was added.
After a further 10 min sodium triacetoxyborohydride (1.54 g, 2.1 eq) was
added and the mixture stirred for 1 h. The mixture was diluted with
CH2Cl2 and washed with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (x 2), dried (MgSO4) and
concentrated to give a 32. tert-Butyl
(1s,4s)-4-(2-(2'-((dimethylamino)methyl)-4'-hydroxybipheny3-yloxy)-5-fluoronicotinamido)cyclohexylcarbamate
37. Prepared from 32 and dimethylamine using General Method J in 95%
yield. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 8.36 (dd, J = 8.2, 3.1 Hz, 1H), 8.10 -
8.02 (m, 2H), 7.49 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.28 - 7.23 (m, 1H), 7.18 - 7.10
(m, 3H), 7.07 - 7.01 (m, 1H), 6.80 (dd, J = 8.3, 2.6 Hz, 1H), 4.46 - 4.37
(m, 1H), 4.24 - 4.10 (m, 1H), 3.67 - 3.54 (m, 1H), 3.39 (s, 2H), 2.16 (s,
6H), 1.92 - 1.63 (m, 8H), 1.42 (s, 9H). LRMS: m/z 579 [M+H]+.
