$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S)-2-(Ethylamino)-1-phenylethanol (14). To a solution of
(S)-2-amino-1-phenylethanol (0.960 g, 7.00 mmol) in EtOH (7.5 mL) cooled
at 0 °C was added acetaldehyde (0.410 mL; 7.31 mmol). After 1 h at 0 °C,
NaBH4 (0.550 g; 14.5 mmol) was added portionwise and the reaction mixture
was stirred at 0 °C for 3 h. The reaction was quenched by addition of
water and 5% NaOH. The reaction mixture was extracted twice with EtOAc.
The organic phases were combined, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel using THF/EtOH/NH4OH (20/1/1) as eluent.
0.785 g (86%) of the title compound as a yellow oil. ESI/APCI(+): 166
(M+H).
