$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthetic procedure for 5-(N-ethyl)amino-3,4-dihydroquinolin-2(1H)-one
(2). The Pd/C (4.62 g, 4.32 mmol) was added to the flask containing
isopropanol (100 ml). Ammonium formate (13.61 g, 215.81 mmol) dissolved
in water (20 ml) was transferred to the same flask. The reaction mixture
was stirred for 5 min to activate Pd/C. Then,
5-amino-3,4-dihydroquinolin-2(1H)-one 1 (7.04 g, 43.16 mmol) was added.
Subsequently, acetaldehyde (5.71 g, 51.79 mmol) was added dropwise, and
the reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3-4 h. The
progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC using silica gel plates.
After completing the reaction, the Pd/C catalyst was filtered off and the
solvent was removed by rotary evaporation. The reaction mixture was
diluted with CH2Cl2 and washed with brine and water. The organic layer
was dried by anhydrous Na2SO4, and evaporated. The product 2 (80 % yield)
as pale yellow powder. Mp = 168-170 °C, IR (KBr disk): ν 3421 (NH), 3055
(=CH), 1678 (C=O), 1346 (C-N); 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 9.80 (s, 1H,
quinolin, -CONH-), 6.92 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H, quinolin-H7), 6.16 (d, J =
8.0 Hz, 1H, quinolin-H8), 6.13 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H, quinolin-H6), 5.20 (s,
1H, NH), 3.38 (q, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H, -CH2-), 2.60 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H,
quinolin-H4), 2.38 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H, quinolin-H3). 0.99 (t, J = 7.1 Hz,
3H, -CH3); 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO) δ 170.13 (quinolin, -CONH-), 140.01
(quinolin, 5-C), 134.71 (quinolin, 9-C),128.44 (quinolin, 7-C), 117.86
(quinolin, 10-C), 116.35 (quinolin, 6-C), 115.22 (quinolin, 8-C), 48.47
(-CH2-), 29.88 (quinolin, 3-C), 20.64 (quinolin, 4-C), 10.39 (-CH3);
LC-MS (ESI): m/z 191 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and biological evaluation of novel quinolin-2(1H)-one
derivatives as potential antimicrobial agents
