$DATUM N,N-Dimethyl-N-tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-ylamine(3). Dimethylamine(4.3kg) was
dissolved in THF (15.1kg) at 0-10 °C. To the resulting solution were
added tetrahydro- 4H-pyran-4-one (12, 3.0 kg) and 5% Pd-C (wet, 0.3 kg)
under nitrogen atmosphere, and the whole was stirred for 4 h under the
conditions of 2 kgf/cm2 hydrogen. After the reaction was completed, Pd-C
was filtered off and washed with THF (5 L). The filtrate and washings
were combined and concentrated at 15-45 °C under reduced pressure (50-100
mmHg). The concentrate was distilled under reduced pressure, the fraction
boiling at 60-80 °C/30-40 mmHg was collected to give 3. Colorless oil,
yield 2.9 kg, 75%. Anal for C7H15NO•H2O. Calcd: C, 64.16; H, 11.70; N,
10.70. Found: C, 64.02; H, 11.44; N,11.03. 1H NMR (CDCl3, δ , 300 MHz)
1.5-1.6 (2H, m), 1.7-1.8 (2H, m), 2.1-2.4 (7H, m), 3.3-3.5 (2H, m),
3.9-4.1 (2H, m). IR (neat, cm-1) 2952, 2836, 2771, 1213, 1135.
