$DATUM 1-(4-ethynylphenyl)-N,N-dimethylmethanamine (S4) Glacial acetic acid (3
drops) was added to a mixture of 4-ethynylbenzaldehyde (1.5 g, 11.6
mmol), dimethylamine (2M in THF, 9.0 mL, 18.0 mmol) and NaBH(OAc)3 (3.7
g, 17.5 mmol) in DCE (40 mL). The resulting mixture was stirred for 2.5 h
at rt. The reaction was quenched with sat. aq. NaHCO3. The product was
extracted into CH2Cl2 (100 mL, then 2 x 50 mL), and the combined organic
layer was washed with brine (25 mL), dried over Na2SO4 and evaporated in
vacuo. Purification by silica gel chromatography (3% 2M NH3-MeOH in
CH2Cl2). 1-(4-ethynylphenyl)-N,N-dimethylmethanamine (1.3 g, 72%). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.46 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.28 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H),
3.42 (s, 2H), 3.07 (s, 1H), 2.24 (s, 6H); LCMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
[C11H13N + H]+ 160.1; found, 159.8.
