$DATUM Methyl 3-(1-Ethy2,2-dimethylhydrazinyl)propanoate (89b). To a solution of
methyl 3-(2,2-dimethylhydrazinyl)propanoate (87) (1.46 g, 10 mmol) and
acetaldehyde (0.66 g, 15 mmol) in methanol (20 mL) was added sodium
cyanoborohydride (1.20 g, 20 mmol) portionwise at room temperature for 10
min. The mixture was stirred overnight and evaporated, and saturated NaCl
(10 mL) was added to the residue. The mixture was extracted with ethyl
acetate (4 x 20 mL), the extract was dried (Na2SO4) and evaporated, and
the residue was disted at 70-75 °C/15 mmHg to afford 89b. Yield 1.18 g
(68%). 1H NMR (CDCl3, HMDSO) δ 1.03 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 6H), 2.26 (s, 6H),
2.45 (q, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 2.48 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H), 2.71 (t, J = 6.6 Hz,
2H), 3.65 (s, 3H). GC-MS (EI, 70 eV) m/z (Irel, %) 87.1 [C4H11N2]+ (100),
145.1 [M - C2H5]+ (9), 159.1 [M - CH3]+ (15), 174.1 M+ (51).
