$DATUM 2,3-Dichloro-N-ethylaniline (10c). A solution of 2,3-dichloroaniline
(10a) (3.00 g, 18.5 mmol) in methanol (20 mL) was treated with 1.0 mL of
acetaldehyde (19 mmol) and 1.4 g of sodium cyanoborohydride (22 mmol).
The resulting mixture was stirred at room temperature for 4 h and then
diluted with chloroform, washed with brine, dried, and concentrated under
vacuum. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography
(n-hexane/ethyl acetate 9:1) to yield pure 10c (2.16 g, 11.4 mmol, 62%
yield) as an oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.31 (t, 3H, J =7.1 Hz), 3.20 (q, 2H,
J =7.1 Hz), 4.35 (br, 1H), 6.54 (dd, 1H, J =8.2, 1.5 Hz), 6.77 (dd, 1H, J
=8.2, 1.5 Hz), 7.06 (t, 1H, J =8.2 Hz); MS m/z 189 (M+, 27), 174 (M+
-CH3, 100).
