$DATUM A mixture of pyridine-4-carboxaldehyde (1.18 g, 11 mmol),
N,N-dimethylamine (0.5 g of gas in 10 mL of MeOH), and a catalytic amount
of 10% Pd/C was hydrogenated at 50 psi for 1 h. The catalyst was removed
by filtration, and the filtrate was evaporated to a viscous oil. A
mixture of the oil and H2O (20 mL) was extracted with Et2O (3 x 25 mL);
the combined ethereal extract was dried (K2CO3), and the solvent was
removed in vacuo to afford 0.38 g (28%) of 29 as its free base after
short-path distillation. 4-(N,N-Dimethylaminomethyl)pyridine (bp 52-53
°C).
