$DATUM 6-N,N-Diethylamino-4-trifluoromethylquinolin-2(1H)-one (4d) To a solution
of 3 (1.0 g, 4.4 mmol) in 100 mL acetic acid were added 6 pellets
(approximately 4.5 g, 0.12 mol) of NaBH4 during a 6 hour period. The
mixture was stirred at rt for 5 days and 100 mL water was carefully
added. The precipitate was filtered and rinsed with water. The yield was
1.1 g almost pure product. Crystallization from MeOH/water 8:1 afforded
pure 4d (0.56 g, 45%) as a yellow solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz,CDCl3) : δ 10.3
(bs, 1H), 7.18 (d, 1H, J = 9.3), 7.07 (dd, 1H, J = 9.3, 2.4), 7.03 (s,
1H), 6.95 (s, 1H), 3.39 (q, 4H, J = 6.8), 1.18 (t, 6H, J = 6.8).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM only monoalkylated product observed in absence of acid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of
6-N,N-Bis(2,2,2-trifluoroethyl)amino-4-trifluoromethylquinolin-2(1H)-one
as a Novel Selective Androgen Receptor Modulator
