$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A mixture of ethyl
3-methy1H-pyrazole-4-carboxylate (2 g, 13 mmol), potassium carbonate (2.7
g, 19.5 mmol) and 2,3- difluorobenzaldehyde (1.56 mL, 14.3 mmol) in DMF
(13 mL) was stirred at 100 °C for 3 h. The mixture was allowed to reach
room temperature and water was added. The compound was extracted with
ethyl acetate. Organic layer was washed with brine, decanted, dried over
magnesium sulfate and solvent evaporated under vacuum to give 3.4 g of
crude material of the title compound (75% purity) was used in the next
step without further purification. Ethyl
1-[2-(dimethylaminomethyl)-6-fluoro-phenyl]-3-methypyrazole-4-carboxylate:
2.0 M dimethylamine in tetrahydrofuran (9.2 mL, 18.4 mmol) and a few
drops of AcOH were added to a solution of the above compound (3.4 g, 9.23
mmol, 75% purity) in tetrahydrofuran (46 mL). The mixture was stirred for
10 min and then sodium triacetoxyborohydride (5.1 g, 23 mmol) was added.
The reaction was stirred at room temperature overnight. The mixture was
diluted with ethyl acetate. The organic layer was separated, washed with
saturated aqueous solution of sodium bicarbonate. The organic layer was
separated, dried over magnesium sulfate and solvent evaporated under
vacuum. The residue was purified by Isco chromatography eluting with
dichloromethane/methanol to give the title compound (two steps). Yield
1.1 g, 28%. LC-MS (ESI) m/z: 306 (M + H)+ tR = 2.05 min, method 2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of a Novel Series of Orally Active Nociceptin/Orphanin FQ (NOP)
Receptor Antagonists Based on a
Dihydrospiro(piperidine-4,7'-thieno[2,3-c]pyran) Scaffold
