$DATUM (R)-6-((3R,4R)-1-Ethyl-3-methyl-piperidin-4-yl)-7-(2-fluoro-phenyl)-4-methyl-2,10-dihyd
ro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one hydrochloride (30). To a
solution of
(R)-7-(2-fluoro-phenyl)-4-methyl-6-((3R,4R)-3-methyl-piperidin-4-yl)-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,
2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one (intermediate obtained at Step F during
preparation of compound 17a, 0.03 g, 0.073 mmol) in MeOH (2 mL) and
acetaldehyde (0.049 g, 0.441 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was
stirred at ambient temperature for 3 h. NaBH3CN (0.014 g, 0.22 mmol) was
added and the reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 0.5
h. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo and the residue was
purified by preparative TLC (eluting with 10% MeOH in dichloromethane).
(R)-6-((3R,4R)-1-ethyl-3-methyl-piperidin-4-yl)-7-(2-fluoro-phenyl)-4-methyl-2,10-dihydro-9
-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one. The product was stirred with HCl
(4M in EtOAc, 10 mL) for 30 min then the reaction mixture was
concentrated in vacuo.
(R)-6-((3R,4R)-1-ethyl-3-methyl-piperidin-4-yl)-7-(2-fluoro-phenyl)-4-methyl-2,10-dihydro-9
-oxa-1,2,4a-triaza-phenanthren-3-one hydrochloride acid (compound 30,
0.0204 g as a white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD): δ 7.44-7.21 (m, 4H),
6.90-6.84 (m, 2H), 4.86-4.85 (m, 1H), 4.63-4.62 (m, 2H), 3.60 (s, 1H),
3.12-2.77 (m, 6H), 2.45 (s, 1H), 1.97-1.89 (m, 2H), 1.48 (m, 3H),
1.30-1.29 (m, 3H), 0.90 (m, 3H). LC/MS (Table 1, Method 4) Rt = 1.851
min.; MS m/z: 437 [M+H]+. SFC (Table 4, Method 4), Rt =1.052 min.
