$DATUM N-Ethyl-3-(5-nitro-1H-indol-3-yl)cyclohexanamine ((±)-32). To a solution
of (±)-29 (1.20 g, 4.65 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (50 mL) was added
AcOH (0.28 mL, 4.65 mmol), EtNH2·HCl (0.38 g, 4.65 mmol), and NaBH(OAc)3
(1.50 g, 7.00 mmol) and the mixture left to stir overnight at rt. Same
workup as in (±)-7. The crude was purified by column chromatography (2 M
NH3 in MeOH:CH2Cl2 1:9). Two diastereomers as yellow solids. trans-(±)-32
(Less Polar Diastereomer): (0.70 g, 52%). cis-(±)-32 (More Polar
Diastereomer): (0.21 g, 16%). trans-(±)-32 (Less Polar Diastereomer): 1H
NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.64 (d, 1H, J = 2.1 Hz), 8.34 (s, 1H, NH), 8.09 (dd, 1H, J
= 2.1, 9.0 Hz), 7.37 (d, 1H, J = 9.0 Hz), 7.12 (d, 1H, J = 2.1 Hz),
3.42-3.24 (m, 1H), 3.06-3.01 (m, 1H), 2.70 (q, 2H, J = 7.2, 7.2 Hz),
2.07-2.01 (m, 2H), 1.82-1.74 (m, 2H), 1.70-1.55 (m, 4H), 1.17 (t, 3H, J =
8.4 Hz). EI-MS (m/z, %) 287 (M+, 10), 242 (100). cis-(±)-32 (More Polar
Diastereomer): 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.61 (d, 1H, J = 2.1 Hz), 8.37 (s, 1H,
NH), 8.10 (dd, 1H, J = 2.1, 9.0 Hz), 7.37 (d, 1H, J = 9.0 Hz), 7.10 (d,
1H, J = 1.8 Hz), 3.00-2.89 (m, 1H), 2.75 (q, 2H, J = 7.2 Hz), 2.32-2.28
(m, 1H), 2.11-2.04 (m, 2H), 1.97-1.84 (m, 1H), 1.63-1.47 (m, 2H),
1.44-1.29 (m, 3H), 1.14 (t, 3H, J = 7.1 Hz). EI-MS (m/z, %) 287 (M+, 15),
244 (100).
