$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-Propylaminopiperidine-1-carboxylic acid benzyl ester (S3). To a
solution of ketone S2 (3.00 g, 12.9 mmol) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (5 mL) was
added n-propylamine (6 mL, 73.1 mmol, 5.7 equiv) and a catalytic amount
of p-toluenesulfonic acid (pTSA, 5 mg). The reaction mixture was stirred
at room temperature for 8 h in the presence of 3 A molecular sieve
(oven-dried, 1 g), before it was filtrated through a pad of Celite,
washed with CH2Cl2 (3 x 20 mL). The filtrate was concentrated in vacuo.
The crude oil was taken up in anhydrous THF (20 mL) and sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (NaBH(OAc)3, 4 g, 18.9 mmol, 1.45 equiv) was added.
The reaction mixture was stirred 8 h at room temperature, before the
solids were removed by filtration through a pad of Celite and washed with
EtOAc (2 x 30 mL). The filtrate was diluted into Et2O (80 mL), washed
with an aqueous saturated NaHCO3 solution (40 mL), water (3 x 50 mL) and
brine (20 mL), dried over Na2SO4, filtrated, and evaporated in vacuo. The
residue was dissolved in a minimum of CH2Cl2 and purified using flash
column chromatography (silica gel, 150 g, CH2Cl2:MeOH:NH4OH, 95:5:0.5 →
90:10:1) to afford amine S3. Yellow oil, yield (2.21 g , quantitative
based on a conversion of 62%). Rf = 0.15 (silica gel, CH2Cl2:MeOH:NH4OH,
95:5:0.5); IR (film) νmax 3307, 2934, 2873, 1694, 1434, 1365, 1275, 1227,
1116, 1027, 764, 698 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 7.35-7.25 (m,
5H), 5.09 (s, 2H), 4.2-4.0 (m, 2H), 2.95-2.75 (m, 2H), 2.65-2.55 (m, 1H),
2.56 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 1.9-1.8 (m, 2H), 1.46 (sixt, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H),
1.35-1.15 (m, 2H), 0.89 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
(ppm): 154.9, 136.5, 128.1, 127.6, 127.4, 66.6, 54.4, 48.4, 42.4, 23.1,
11.5; HRMS calcd. for C16H25N2O2 [M+H]+: 277.19105, found: 277.19135; MS
(ESI) [M+H]+ 277.2.
