$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2.5 Synthesis of compound 6 Step 1: A mixture of 1-propanamine (2.60 g,
44.0 mmol), sodium sulfate (5.68 g, 40.0 mmol) and
4-(trifluoromethyl)benzaldehyde (6.96 g, 40.0 mmol) in dichloromethane
(DCM) (50 mL) was stirred at RT for 3 days. Sodium sulfate was filtered
off. DCM was removed in vacuo. The obtained crude imine was dissolved in
methanol (50 mL). NaBH4 (0.76 g, 20.0 mmol) was added slowly. The
reaction was stirred under N2. After 1.5 hours, the reaction finished.
Solvent was removed under reduced pressure and the residue was
partitioned between DCM and water. The aqueous phase was washed with DCM
twice. The combined organic layers were washed with sat. NaHCO3 solution
and brine. The mixture was then dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. After
filtration, solvent was removed in vacuo to afford
N-{[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]methyl}-1-propanamine which was used
without further purification. Colorless oil (8.20 g, 37.7 mmol, 94 %
yield). LCMS: rt = 1.881 minutes, MH+ = 218.1.
