$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2.1 Synthesis of compound 2 Step 1: To a solution of 1-propanamine
propylamine (2.60 g, 44.0 mmol), benzaldehyde (4.24 g, 40.0 mmol) in
dichloromethane (DCM) (50 mL) was added sodium sulfate (5.68 g, 40.0
mmol). The suspension was stirred at RT ovenight. Na2SO4 was filtered off
and then DCM was removed. To the obtained oil was added methanol (50 mL)
and NaBH4 (0.76 g, 20.0 mmol) at 0 °C. After stirring at RT for 45
minutes, the reaction was quenched by sat. NaHCO3 solution. MeOH was
removed under reduced pressure and the residue was partitioned between
DCM and water. The aqueous phase was washed with DCM for 3 times. The
combined organics were washed with brine and then dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4. After filtration, solvent was removed in vacuo to afford
N-(phenylmethyl)-1-propanamine. 5.09 g, 34.1 mmol, 85 % yield. LCMS: rt =
2.416 minutes, MH+ = 150.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
