$DATUM 1-Ethynyl-4-propylaminocyclohexan-1-ol (5). To an ice-cooled suspension
of NaBH(OAc)3 (5.68 g, 26.8 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (40 mL) was added slowly a
solution of 4 (1.48 g, 10.7 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (20 mL), propylamine (3.5 mL,
42.9 mmol), and glacial acetic acid (0.67 mL, 11.77 mmol). The mixture
was allowed to warm to room temperature and stirred for 4 h. Then the
reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 and basified to pH 12
by 6 N NaOH. The aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined
organic layers were dried (MgSO4) and evaporated under reduced pressure.
Purification by flash chromatography (CH2Cl2 + 5% MeOH saturated with
NH3). 5 as a white solid (1.55 g, 80%). Mp 72 °C. IR: 3306, 2936, 2858,
2823, 2676, 2104, 1457, 1371, 1259, 1226, 1132, 1106, 1074, 969, 928,
907, 835 cm-1. 1H NMR (360 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.92 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3 H),
1.41-1.64 (m, 5 H), 1.70-1.80 (m, 1 H), 1.89-2.05 (m, 4 H), 2.40-2.61 (m,
4 H). 13C NMR (360 MHz, CDCl3) δ 11.82, 23.53, 28.00, 30.36, 36.90,
38.46, 49.27, 55.72, 73.02, 86.95. APCI-MS m/z 182 [M+ + 1].
