$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 4: The mixture of 1-propanamine (0.4 mL, 4.84 mmol), sodium sulfate
(0.63 g, 4.47 mmol) and
2-[4-(ethylsulfonyl)phenyl]-N-(4-formylphenyl)acetamide (1.48 g, 4.47
mmol) in dichloromethane (DCM) (30 mL) was stirred at RT for 3 days.
Solvent and excess reagents were removed under vacuum. The obtained crude
imine was dissolved in methanol (30 mL). NaBH4 (0.08 g, 2.23 mmol) was
added slowly. The reaction was stirred under N2. Solvent was removed
under reduced pressure and the residue was partitioned between DCM and
water. The organic layer was washed with sat. NaHCO3 solution and brine.
Solvent was removed in vacuo to afford
2-[4-(ethylsulfonyl)phenyl]-N-{4-[(propylamino)methyl]phenyl}acetamide,
which was used in the next steps without further purification. Yellowish
solid (1.47 g, 3.14 mmol, 70.3 % yield). LCMS: rt = 2.772 minutes, MH- =
373.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
