$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-Methoxy-N-propyl-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalen-2-amine (2). Into a
stirring solution of n-propylamine (14.9 mL, 181.6 mmol) and ketone 1
(12.8 g, 72.6 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (70 mL) was added glacial acetic acid (17.3
mL, 290.5 mmol). After the mixture was stirred for 0.5 h, NaCNBH3 (11.4
g, 181.6 mmol) was added portionwise at 0 °C, followed by methanol (20
mL). The mixture was allowed to reach room temperature and stirred
overnight. The reaction mixture was quenched with a saturated NaHCO3
solution at 0 °C and extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 100 mL). The
combined organic layer was washed with water, brine and dried over
Na2SO4. Solvent was removed under reduced pressure. Crude product was
purified by column chromatography (EtOAc/MeOH, 9:1) to give compound 2.
Yield 11.1 g, 70%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 0.96 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H),
1.54- 1.65 (m, 3H), 2.09-2.16 (m, 1H), 2.52-2.74 (m, 4H), 2.88-3.07 (m,
3H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 6.66 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 6.71 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H),
7.09 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
