$DATUM (±)-N1,N2-Dipropyl-1,2-di(pyridin-2-yl)ethane-1,2-diamine [(±)-1]. A
reactor was charged with NaBH(OAc)3 (763 g, 3.60 mol) and CH2Cl2 (4 L).
The mantle temperature was set at 20 °C, and DIPEA (836 mL, 4.80 mol) was
added, followed by the addition of propionaldehyde (871 mL, 12.0 mol). A
solution of (±)-2 × 2HCl (396 g, 87% w/w, 1.20 mol) and DIPEA (836 mL,
4.80 mol) in CH2Cl2 (10 L) was added over 30 min, and the stirring was
continued for 1 h. Water (2.0 L) and 3.8 M HCl (6 L) were added to the
resulting crude mixture of compound 7 over 35 min, and the stirring was
continued for 30 min. To the aqueous layer was added 1-propanethiol (650
mL, 7.18 mol). The resulting mixture was stirred at 60 °C for 4 h and at
20 °C for an additional 5 h. The mixture was washed with CH2Cl2 (2 × 5
L). To the aqueous layer was added a solution of 3.8 M NaOH (10 L) over
40 min. The resulting emulsion (pH 11) was heated to 30 °C and extracted
with CH2Cl2 (3 × 2.5 L). The combined organic layers were concentrated to
yield diamine (±)-1. The NMR and MS data were in accordance with those
given for (S,S)-1 below. Brown oil, yield 81%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
0.84 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 6H), 1.38-1.51 (m, 4H), 2.31-2.41 (m, 4H), 3.86 (s,
2H), 6.89-6.92 (m, 2H), 6.97- 7.01 (m, 2H), 7.34-7.39 (m, 2H), 8.45-8.47
(m, 2H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 11.8, 23.4, 50.0. 69.3, 121.7,
123.4, 135.5, 149.2, 161.6. HRMS (ESI+): m/z 299.2246 [(M + H)+, calcd
for C18H27N4 299.2236]. [α ]D 20 -1 (c = 1, CH3CN), dr 98:2, ee >99%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Evaluation and Development of Practical Routes to an Enantiomerically
Pure C2-Symmetric Diamine Building Block
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Karlsson, Staffan; Lindberg, Jan; Soerensen, Henrik
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2013), 17(12), 1552-1560

