$DATUM N2,N5-Bis[(R)-1-(benzyloxy)-3-hydroxy-1-oxopropan-2-yl]-3,6-bis(propylamino)pyrazine-2,5-dicarboxamide
(8a). To a solution of the bis-benzyl ester 4d (0.890 g, 1.61 mmol) and
propionaldehyde (5, 0.460 mL, 6.44 mmol) in anhyd DCE (65 mL) was added
HOAc (0.368 mL, 6.44 mmol) with stirring at 0 °C under argon atmosphere.
Then Na(OAc)3BH (1.36 g, 6.44 mmol) was introduced in small portions and
the reddish suspension was slowly allowed to warm to rt and stirred
overnight (ca. 24 h) under argon. The reaction was quenched by a slow
addition of satd NaHCO3 at 0 °C and extracted with CHCl3 (150 mL). The
CHCl3 extracts were successively washed with H2Oand brine (50 mL each).
Removal of the solvent gave 1.04 g of a red solid, which upon flash
chromatography over silica gel [CHCl3-MeOH (39:1, v/v)] afforded 8a
(0.800 g, 78%) as a dark-red solid.
N2,N5-Bis[(R)-1-(benzyloxy)-3-hydroxy-1-oxopropan-2-yl]-3,6-bis(propylamino)pyrazine-2,5-dicarboxamide
(8a), yield 0.800 g, 78%. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.68 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 2 H),
7.60 (t, J = 5.6 Hz, 2 H), 7.37-7.33 (m, 10 H), 5.26 (s, 4 H), 4.78-4.75
(dt, J = 7.3, 3.7 Hz, 2 H), 4.08 (dd, J = 6.1, 3.9 Hz, 4 H), 3.39-3.28
(m, 4 H), 2.64 (t, J = 6.2 Hz, 2 H), 1.65-1.61 (m, 4 H), 0.97 (t, J = 7.4
Hz, 6 H). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 169.9, 166.5, 146.0, 135.1, 128.7, 128.6,
128.2, 125.8, 67.6, 63.6, 55.1, 42.9, 22.7, 11.7. RP-LC/MS (ESI) m/z
637.4 (M + H)+ (tR = 5.13 min, 5-95% B/6 min). Anal. Calcd for
C32H40N6O8: C, 60.37; H, 6.33; N, 13.20. Found: C, 60.49; H, 6.42; N,
13.13.
