$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Ethyl
1-alkyl-4-phenyl-1,2,5,6-tetrahydropyridine-3-carboxylate 41. A mixture
of 14 (2 g, 8.65 mmol), NaCNBH3 (1.63 g, 25.95 mmol), aldehyde
(paraformaldehyde, propionaldehyde, or butyraldehyde), and EtOH (20 mL)
was stirred at room temperature overnight followed by standard aqueous
workup. The crude product was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (2:1 hexanes:EtOAc) to afford 41. Ethyl
1-n-propyl-4-phenyl-1,2,5,6-tetrahydropyridine-3-carboxylate 41b.
Colorless oil, 1.45 g, 61% yield 1H NMR (300 MHz): δ 7.23-7.36 (m, 3H),
7.13 (dd, J = 7.5, 1.8 Hz, 2H), 3.89 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 3.37 (t, J =
2.7 Hz, 2H), 2.71 (t, J = 5.4 Hz, 2H), 2.50-2.62 (m, 4H), 1.83 (m, 2H),
0.96 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 3H), 0.86 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H) ppm; EI-MS m/z 273
(M+).
