hydrochloride acid (0.300, 0.761 mmol) and paraformaldehyde (0.228 g,
7.61 mmol) and the reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature
for 4 h. Then sodium cyanoborohydride (0.096 g, 1.52 mmol) was added and
the reaction mixture was stirred for 30 min. The solvent was removed in
vacuo and the residue was purified by prep-TLC (eluting with 10% MeOH in
DCM).
(R)-7-(2-fluoro-phenyl)-4-methyl-6-(1-methyl-piperidin-4-yl)-2,10-dihydro-9-oxa-1,2,4a-tria
za-phenanthren-3-one (compound 26, 0.160 g, 51%) as a white solid. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CD3OD) δ 7.50-7.41 (m, 1H), 7.32-7.26 (m, 2H), 7.25-7.19 (m,
1H), 7.09 (s, 1H), 6.86 (s, 1H), 5.02-4.93 (m, 1H), 4.70-4.59 (m, 2H),
3.63-3.46 (m, 2H), 3.04-2.89 (m, 2H), 2.84 (s, 3H), 2.76 (m, 1H),
2.28-2.01 (m, 3H), 1.96-1.83 (m, 1H), 1.52 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H). LCMS
(Table 1, Method 4) Rt = 1.617 min; MS m/z: 409 [M+H]+. SFC (Table 4,
Method 13) Rt = 3.630 min.
