$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure F To a solution of a morpholin-2-one (1.0 eq) in THF (5
mL/mmol) and CH3CN (14 mL/mmol) was added an aldehyde or a ketone (5.0
eq). After 15 min at room temperature, NaBH3CN (2.0 eq) was added
portionwise. The reaction mixture was stirred for an additional 15 min
and acetic acid (2.1 eq) was added. The reaction mixture was stirred at
room temperature for 1-18 h. The reaction was quenched by addition of
saturated NaHCO3. The reaction mixture was diluted with EtOAc and the
phases were separated. The organic phase was washed with water and brine,
dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated. The residue was purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel to give the desired compound.
2-(6,6-Dimethyl-2-oxo-4-propylmorpholin-3-yl)-N-(4-isopropylphenyl)acetamide
(46). The compound was prepared according to the procedure F from 44
(0.080 g; 0.263 mmol), propionaldehyde (0.095 mL; 1.33 mmol), NaBH3CN
(0.033 g; 0.525 mmol) and acetic acid (0.031 mL; 0.542 mmol) in THF (1.4
mL) and CH3CN (3.8 mL). Purification by flash chromatography on silica
gel using a gradient of EtOAc (20 to 70%) in heptane. 0.036 g (40%) of
the title compound as a white powder. ESI/APCI(+): 347 (M+H); 369 (M+Na);
715 (2M+Na). ESI/APCI(-): 345 (M-H). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 8.45 (1H,
s); 7.41 (2H, m); 7.16 (2H, d); 3.37 (1H, m); 2.8-3.1 (5H, m); 2.34 (2H,
m); 1.55 (2H, m); 1.47 (3H, s); 1.41 (3H, s); 1.22 (6H, d); 0.94 (3H, t).
