$DATUM tert-butyl 4-isopropyl-1,4-diazepane-1-carboxylate (45).
1-Boc-hexahydro-1,4-diazepine (0.500 g, 2.50 mmol) and acetone (366 μL, 5
mmol) were dissolved in dry MeOH, activated molecular sieves (3Å) were
added, and the solution was stirred for 5 minutes under N2. A solution of
1.25 M HCl in MeOH (400 μL, 0.50 mmol) and NaBH3CN (0.110 g, 1.75 mmol)
were added to the solution and the mixture stirred for 20 hours. The
reaction mixture became turbid. The reaction was filtered, the solvent
evaporated under reduced pressure and the residue extracted with
AcOEt/NaHCO3 sat which was used without further purification. a colorless
oil (0.561 g, 93% yield). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) mixture of 2 rotamers δ
3.46-3.30 (m, 4H), 2.83 (sep, J= 6 Hz, 1H), 2.62-2.46 (m, 4H), 1.78-1.62
(m, 2H), 1.39 (s, 4.5H), 1.39 (s, 4.5H), 0.94 (d, J= 6 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 75 MHz) mixture of 2 rotamers δ 155.5 (C), 155.4 (C), 78.9 (C),
55.3 (CH), 55.1 (CH), 52.0 (CH2), 51.5 (CH2), 50.4 (CH2), 48.1 (CH2),
47.7 (CH2), 45.8 (CH2), 44.9 (CH2), 28.6 (CH2), 28.5 (CH2), 28.4 (CH3),
18.3 (CH3), 18.3 (CH3); MS (ESI+) m/z 243.2 ([[M+1]+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
