$DATUM (9e) tert-Butyl
4-({5-[3-(acetylamino)but-1-ynyl]-1,3-thiazol-2-yl}oxy)phenylcarbamate
(2.85g, 7.0 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (35 ml) and TFA (8.75 ml, 25%
v/v) was added via syringe. After 4 h of stirring at rt, the reaction
solution was concentrated by rotary evaporation and then placed on high
vacuum for 2h to give a light yellow solid which was used in the next
step without further purification. A portion of the crude product from
above (500 mg, 1.7 mmol) was dissolved in a buffer solution prepared from
NaOAc / HOAc in MeOH (6 ml). To this solution was added acetone (0.374
ml, 5.1 mmol) followed by NaCNBH3 (320 mg, 5.1 mmol). The reaction was
heated to 70oC in a water bath for 1 h. The reaction solution was cooled
and MeOH was evaporated. The residue was taken up in EtOAc and quenched
with water. The layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted
once with EtOAc. The combined organics was dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
concentrated. The residue was purified by flash column chromatography to
give 9e (340 mg, 66%) as a hydroscopic white solid.
N-{3-[2-(4-Isopropylamino-phenoxy)-thiazol-5-yl]-1-methyl-prop-2-ynyl}-acetamide
(9e), Yield (340 mg, 66%) 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ ppm 1.06 - 1.20 (d,
J = 6.0 Hz, 6 H), 1.31 (d, J=6.99 Hz, 3 H), 1.80 (s, 3 H), 3.52 (m, 1 H),
4.70 - 4.88 (m, 1 H), 5.64 (d, J=7.72 Hz, 1 H), 6.52 - 6.65 (d, J = 9.0
Hz, 2 H), 7.00 - 7.13 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2 H,) 7.46 (s, 1 H), 8.39 (d,
J=7.72 Hz, 1 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 21.5, 22.3, 36.2, 43.2,
70.8, 96.4, 110.8, 112.7, 121.2, 142.5, 144.9, 147.0, 168.1, 174.6; HRMS
(TOF) calc for C18H21N3O2S: 344.13545 [(M + H+)]; found: 344.14285; calcd
for C18H19N3O2S: C, 62.95; H, 6.16; N, 12.23; found: C, 62.45, H, 5.67,
N, 11.97.
