$DATUM N'-Isopropyl-3-[(3,5-dimethylphenyl)sulfonyl]-5-chloro-1H-indole-
2-carboxyhydrazide (9, RS 1833). Sodium cyanoborohydride (0.196 g, 0.0031
mol) was added to an ice-cooled mixture of acetone (0.15 g, 0.19 mL,
0.0026 mol) and 5-chloro-3-[(3,5-dimethylphenyl)
sulfonyl]-1H-indole-2-carbohydrazide (0.98 g, 0.0026 mol) in methanol/THF
(1:1, 32.5 mL) containing 6 N HCl/methanol (1: 1. 0.44 mL). The reaction
was stirred at room temperature overnight. The mixture was reduced to a
small volume, diluted with water, and extracted with ethyl acetate. The
organic layer was washed with brine and dried. Removal of the solvent
gave a crude product which was purified on silica gel column
(chloroform/ethanol 95:5) to give 9 (0.69 g, 63%). Mp: 248-250 °C (from
ethanol). 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6): δ 1.09 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 6H), 2.34 (s, 6H),
3.15 (m, 1H), 5.19 (br s, 1H, disappeared on treatment with D2O), 7.25
(s, 1H), 7.33 (dd, J = 2.0 and 8.7 Hz, 1H), 7.53 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 1H),
7.67 (s, 2H), 7.89 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 10.25 (br s, 1H, disappeared on
treatment with D2O), 13.05 (br s, 1H, disappeared on treatment with D2O).
IR (Nujol): ν 1620, 3230, 3300 cm-1. Anal. Calcd (C20H22ClN3O3S (419.96))
C, H, Cl, N, S.
