$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6-Isopropylaminohexanoic Acid
{8-[(6-Isopropylaminohexanoyl)methylamino]octyl}methylamide (40). A
solution of 2914 (1.12 g, 2.8 mmol) in acetone (50 mL) was hydrogenated
over 10% Pd on charcoal for 4 h. Following catalyst removal, the solvent
was evaporated, obtaining a residue that was purified by flash
chromatography. Elution with MeOH/aqueous 28% ammonia (9:1) afforded 40
as an oil: 30% yield 6-Isopropylaminohexanoic Acid
{8-[(6-Isopropylaminohexanoyl)methylamino]octyl}methylamide (40), 30%
yield 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.02 (d, 12H), 1.20-1.69 (m, 24H), 2.15-2.38 (m,
4H + 2H exchangeable with D2O),2.57 (t, 4H), 2.66-2.86 (m, 2H) 2.90 (s,
3H), 2.98 (s, 3H), 3.16- 3.38 (m, 4H); EI MS m/z 482 (M+).
