$DATUM (R)-methyl 1-isopropylpyrrolidine-2-carboxylate (34). To a solution of
D-proline methyl ester hydrochloride (1g, 6 mmol) in MeOH (60 mL), were
added sequentially NaHCO3 (2g, 24 mmol), Acetone (0.680 mL, 9 mmol) and
NaBH(OAc)3 (2.54 g, 12 mmol). The reaction mixture was then stirred for
48 hours at room temperature. The mixture was extracted with Et2O, the
organic layers were washed with brine, dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
evaporated under reduced pressure. The desired compound was directly used
in the next step, without further purification. (R)-methyl
1-isopropylpyrrolidine-2-carboxylate (34). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 3.69
(s, 3H), 3.43-3.38 (m, 1H), 3.13-3.06 (m, 1H), 2.81-2.73 (m, 1H),
2.61-2.53 (q, J = 6 Hz, 1H), 2.11-2.02 (m, 1H), 1.95-1.73 (m, 3H), 1.05
(d, J= 6 Hz, 6H) ; MS (ESI+) m/z 172.1 ([[M+1]+); HRMS (ESI+) calcd. for
C9H18N2O 172.1332 ([[M+1]+]) found 172.1333.
