$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (2S)-2-[[(3β,15α,16α,23R,24S)-16,23-Epoxy-24-ethoxy-15,25-dihydroxy-9,19-cyclolanostan-3-yl]oxy]-4-(1-isopropylazetidin-3-yl)morpholine
(1). A solution of 7 (9.784 g, 14.86 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (110 mL) and EtOH
(15 mL) was treated with acetone (5.5 mL, 74.3 mmol, 5 equiv) and
NaBH(OAc)3 (9.44 g, 44.6 mmol, 3 equiv), and the reaction mixture was
stirred at RT, using LC−MS to monitor the reaction progress. After 1 h,
the reaction mixture was poured into CH2Cl2 (700 mL) and saturated
NaHCO3(aq) (100 mL), and the phases were separated. The aqueous layer was
extracted with CH2Cl2 (250 mL), and then the combined organic layers were
dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The
crude residue was purified using C18 silica chromatography (gradient
elution, 10−45% CH3CN/H2O + 0.1% formic acid), and the pure
product-containing fractions were combined and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was taken up in CH2Cl2, washed with 3 M NaOH(aq)
(10 mL, 30 mmol) and brine, dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated
under reduced pressure to provide 1 in free-base form as a yield over two
steps; 23.5% overall yield from 2 when corrected for purity of the
starting material).
(2S)-2-[[(3β,15α,16α,23R,24S)-16,23-Epoxy-24-ethoxy-15,25-dihydroxy-9,19-cyclolanostan-3-yl]oxy]-4-(1-isopropylazetidin-3-yl)morpholine
(1). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 4.59 (dd, J = 6.4, 2.4 Hz, 1H, C33), 3.94
(dt, J = 11.6, 3.4 Hz, 1H, C36), 3.90 (dt, J = 11.6, 3.4 Hz, 1H, C23),
3.81 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H, C15), 3.73 (m, 1H, C31), 3.67 (m, 1H, C31), 3.62
(m, 1H, C36), 3.46 (m, 1H, C39), 3.45 (m, 1H, C38), 3.45 (m, 1H, C16),
3.16 (dd, J = 11.6, 4.5 Hz, 1H, C3), 2.95 (d, J = 2.9 Hz, 1H, C24), 2.94
(p, J = 6.2 Hz, 1H, C37), 2.88 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H, C39), 2.84 (t, J = 6.7
Hz, 1H, C38), 2.65 (d, J = 11.0 Hz, 1H, C34), 2.43 (dt, J = 11.4, 3.0 Hz,
1H, C35), 2.34 (sept, J = 6.2 Hz, 1H, C40), 2.15 (m, 1H, C35), 2.09 (m,
1H, C2), 2.05 (m, 1H, C34), 1.90 (m, 1H, CH2), 1.75 (m, 1H, C20), 1.71
(m, 2H, CH2), 1.68 (m, 1H, CH2), 1.57 (m, 1H, C1), 1.54 (m, 2H, CH2),
1.53 (m, 2H, CH2), 1.52 (m, 1H, C17), 1.47 (m, 2H, C22), 1.26 (t, J = 7.0
Hz, 3H, C32), 1.26 (s, 6H, C26, C27), 1.23 (m, 2H, CH2), 1.16 (m, 1H,
C2), 1.02 (s, 3H, C18), 0.97 (s, 3H, C30), 0.93 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3H, C21),
0.93 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 6H, C41, C42), 0.91 (s, 3H, C28), 0.81 (s, 3H, C29),
0.78 (m, 1H, C1), 0.60 (d, J = 3.9 Hz, 1H, C19), 0.34 (d, J = 4.3 Hz, 1H,
C19). The methylene protons of C5, C6, C7, C8, C11, and C12 correspond to
the signals at δ 1.90, 1.71, 1.68, 1.54, 1.54, 1.53, and 1.23 but could
not be def initively assigned. 13C NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 100.7 (C33),
88.5 (C3), 86.7 (C37), 81.8 (C16), 80.7 (C23), 75.4 (C15), 73.4 (C25),
70.3 (C31), 63.0 (C36), 58.5 (C40), 57.1 (C38), 57.0 (C39), 54.2 (C24),
54.1 (C8), 53.8 (C34), 51.8 (C14), 49.0 (C35), 48.2 (C17), 47.4 (C5),
42.3 (C4), 40.8 (C13), 38.2, 33.2 (C20), 31.9, 31.6, 31.2 (C19), 29.2,
27.2 (C27), 27.0 (C26), 26.7 (C2), 26.6 (C10), 26.4 (C22), 25.6 (C28),
20.8 (C1), 19.7 (C21), 19.6 (C9), 19.6 (C41), 19.6 (C42), 19.4 (C18),
15.7 (C32), 14.9 (C29), 13.3 (C30). The four signals at δ 38.2, 31.9,
31.6, and 29.2 correspond to C6, C7, C11, and C12 but could not be def
initively assigned. MS (ESI+): m/z = 701 [M + H]+. Crystal data. formula:
C42H77.46N2O8.73; formula weight: 750.20; space group: P1 (No. 1); a:
7.0634(4)Å; b: 7.5583(6)Å; c: 20.2487(15)Å; α: 84.412(6)deg;
β:89.357(6)deg; γ: 79.592(6): V: 1058.16(13)Å3; Z: 1; dcalc: 1.177g cm-3;
crystal dimensions: 0.20 x 0.12 x 0.10mm.
