$DATUM (R)-4-Ethyl-6-phenylmorpholin-2-one (22). To a mixture of a 40% glyoxal
solution in water (0.636 mL; 5.60 mmol) and toluene (2 mL) cooled at 10
°C was added a solution of (R)-2-(ethylamino)-1-phenylethanol (15)1
(0.900 g; 5.45 mmol) in toluene (2.6 mL). After 2 h at 10 °C, the
reaction mixture was heated at reflux to azeotrope out solvents. The
residue was partitioned between EtOAc and water. The organic phase was
washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated under
reduced pressure. Purification by flash chromatography on silica gel
using a gradient of EtOAc (20 to 50%) in heptane. 0.638 g (57%) of the
title compound as an orange oil. ESI/APCI(+): 206 (M+H).
