$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
compounds 8a-e (preparation of 8d as representative): Aldehyde 5 (300 mg,
0.7 mmol), 4-aminoquinoline 7d (330 mg, 1.4 mmol), and glacial acetic
acid (0.1 mL) in CH2Cl2 (50 mL) were stirred at room temperature for 30
min. NaBH(OAc)3 (330 mg, 1.03 mmol) was added portionwise for over 3 h
and the reaction mixture was stirred for another 6 h. The reaction
mixture was quenched with water (50 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 30
mL), solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the crude product
was purified by column chromatography over silica gel to furnish Acetic
acid
3-acetoxy-17-(2-butylamino-1-methyl-ethyl)-10,13-dimethylhexadecahydro-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-12-yl
ester (8c), yield 53%. IR (KBr, cm-1) 3342; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ:
0.79 (s, 3H), 0.91 (s, 3H), 0.99 (d, 3H, J = 7.2 Hz), 1.06-1.83 (m, 30H),
2.03 (s, 3H), 2.10 (s, 3H), 2.37 (t, 2H, J = 10.0 Hz), 2.80 (bd, 1H, J =
11.4 Hz), 3.02-3.09 (m, 1H), 4.70 (m, 1H), 5.07 (bs, 1H); FAB-MS (m/z):
490 [M + H]+, 430 [M + H - AcOH]+, 370 [M + H - 2 AcOH]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
