$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure B To a mixture of a 40% glyoxal solution in water (1.0
eq) and toluene (0.5 mL/mmol) cooled at 10 °C was added a solution of an
aminoalcohol (1.0 eq) in toluene (0.3 mL/mmol). After 2-3 h at 10 °C, the
reaction mixture was heated at reflux to azeotrope out solvents. The
residue was purified by distillation under reduced pressure to afford the
desired morpholinone. (S)-4-Ethyl-6-methylmorpholin-2-one (19). The
compound was prepared according to the procedure B from 40% glyoxal
(0.790 mL; 6.95 mmol) and 12 (0.692 g; 6.71 mmol) in toluene (4 mL).
Purification by distillation under reduced pressure. 0.508 g (53%) of the
title compound as a colourless liquid. ESI/APCI(+): 144 (M+H).
