$DATUM N-(2-Chloroethyl)-2-nitrobenzylamine (6).- A solution of
2-nitrobenzaldehyde (300 g, 2 mol) and 2-chloroethylamine hydrochloride
(248 g, 2.16 mol) in ethanol (1.5 L) was stirred for 3 h at ambient
temperature. KBH4 (49.8 g, 0.92 mol) was then added slowly at 0-100 °C in
four portions at intervals of 10 min and stirring continued for 2 h. The
reaction mixture was evaporated to give an oil and a saturated aqueous
sodium hydrogen carbonate was added to the mixture to adjust the pH of
the solution to 9-10, and extracted with methylene chloride (3 x 300 mL).
The combined organic layers were washed with brine (500 mL), and dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4. After removal of the drying agent, the solvent was
evaporated under reduced pressure and the residue, so obtained, was
treated with HCl(g)/ethanol. 7 as the colorless crystalline hydrochloride
(447 g, 90%). An analytical sample was obtained by recrystalization from
ethanol. mp ~210°C (dec.). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 8.20 (d, 1H, J = 8.2 Hz),
7.87 (m, 2H); 7.71 (t, 1H, J = 7.3Hz), 4.50 (s, 1H); 3.99 (t, 1H, J = 6.1
Hz), 3.42 (t, 1H, J = 6.3 Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3): 39.18, 47.33, 48.53,
125.28, 127.04, 130.77, 133.47, 134.33, 148.43. HRMS (EI): Exact Mass:
Calcd for C9H10ClN2O2 213.0431. Found 213.0423. Anal. Calcd for
C9H12Cl2N2O2: C, 43.05; H, 4.82; N, 11.16. Found: C, 43.22; H, 4.82, N,
10.99.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM slow addition of borohydride in 4 portions with 10 min. intervals stage
1, gaseous HCl used stage 4, scalable (450 g scale)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A practical synthesis of
4-acetyl-2,3,4,5-tetrahydro-1H-1,4-benzodiazepine
