$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of the
Diaminopyrimidine.To a solution of 4-nitrophenylacetonitrile (10.0 g,
61.7 mmol), triethylamine(14.5 g, 144 mmol), and
4-(dimethylamino)pyridine (800 mg, 6.56 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (150 mL) at 0 °C
was added propionyl chloride (12.0 g, 64.8 mmol) over 30 min. The
resulting mixture was warmed to room temperature, stirred for 2h, and
concentrated in vacuo. The mixture was extracted in ethylacetate (1 x 150
mL) and washed with saturated NaHCO3 (1 x 80 mL), aqueous HCl (1 x 80
mL), and brine (1 x 80 mL). The organic layer was dried over MgSO3 and
concentrated in vacuo to provide crude butyronitrile (19.g). To a
solution of nitrile (9.72 g, 31.4 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (80 mL) was slowly
added a solution of 2 M trimethylsilyldiazomethane (TMSCHN2) in
diethylether (30 mL, 60 mmol). The reaction was monitored by TLC using an
aliquot to which had been added 3 M HOAc and was extracted in EtOAc.
Glacial HOAc (5 mL) was added dropwise until the excess TMSCHN2 was
consumed as indicated by the absence of N2 evolution. The mixture was
concentrated in vacuo, extracted with EtOAc (1 x 100 mL), and washed with
1 M HOAc (1 x 150 mL) and brine (1 x 100 mL). The organic layer was dried
over MgSO2 and concentrated in vacuo to provide but-2-enenitrile (10.2
g).To a solution of but-2-enenitrile (10.2 g, 31.4 mmol) in EtOH (60 mL)
was added a premixed solution of guanidine hydrochloride (3.605 g, 37.5
mmol) in EtOH (60 mL) and 2.65 M NaOEt in EtOH (14.2 mL, 37.6 mmol). The
resulting dark, purple solution was heated atreflux for 3 h, concentrated
in vacuo, extracted with EtOAc (1 x 150 mL), and washed with 0.5 M NaOH
(2 x 100 mL). The mixture was stirred vigorously, then the resulting
precipitate was filtered, providing pyrimidine-2,4-diamine. To a solution
of 20 wt % Pd(OH)2/C (wet, 600 mg) in MeOH (140 mL) was added
pyrimidine-2,4-diamine (5.00 g, 14.25 mmol) in a heavy walled high
pressure reaction vessel. The vessel was charged with H2 (60psi), and the
mixture was stirred at room temperature for 14 h.The reaction mixture was
filtered through a nylon membrane, and the solution was concentrated in
vacuo followed by trituration with MeOH (20 mL).
6-Ethyl-5-[4-(4-trifluoromethanesulfonyl-benzylamino)-phenyl]-pyrimidine-2,4-diamine,
yield 71%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 8.12 (d, J = 8.5Hz, 2H), 7.85 (d,
J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 6.87 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 6.63(d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 6.54
(t, J = 6.1 Hz, 1H), 5.72 (s, 2H), 5.27(bs, 2H), 4.50 (d, J = 6.1 Hz,
2H), 2.11 (q, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 0.94(t, J = 7.5 Hz, 3H). MS (ESI) m/z )
452 [M + H]+, 450 [M -H]-. Anal. (C20H20F3N5O2S.0.1CF3CO2H) C, H, N.
