$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-N-Ethyl-3,2',6'-tri-N-acetylsisomicin (3). To glacial
acetic acid (1.8 L, 32 mol) in chloroform (4 L) was slowly added sodium
borohydride (300 g, 8 mol) at 20°C. The addition rate was adjusted by
observing the generation rate of hydrogen gas. To this solution, a
solution of 3,2',6'-tri-N-acetylsisomicin (573 g, 1 mol) solution in
chloroform (5 L) was added, and the mixture was stirred for 20 h at 40 ±
5°C. After being cooled to room temperature, the resulting solution was
neutralized with saturated sodium hydroxide solution. This neutralized
solution was diluted with ethanol (5 L), extracted with chloroform (5 L),
and distilled in vacuo. The residue was chromatographed on a column of
silica gel (2.5 kg) with 30:10:1 chloroform: methanol: 14% ammonia water
as eluant. Fractions were collected, concentrated, and lyophilized to
give the title compound 3 as an ivory powder (578 g, 96%).
1-N-Ethyl-3,2',6'-tri-N-acetylsisomicin, yield (578 g, 96%). MS (FAB) 602
(M + H+); 1H NMR (D2O, 300 MHz) δ 1.27 (t, 3H, J= 6.79 Hz, CH2CH3) 1.34
(s, 3H, C-CH3), 1.68- 1.78 (m, 2H), 1.96 (s, 3H), 2.00 (s, 3H), 2.02 (s,
3H), 2.12 (m, 1H), 2.31 (m, 1H), 2.91 (m, 1H), 2.92 (s, 3H, N-CH3), 3.08
(m, 1H), 3.26 (m, 1H), 3.47-3.51 (m, 3H), 3.64-4.00 (m, 8H), 4.23-4.27
(dd, 1H, J= 3.36 Hz, 10.73 Hz), 5.05 (d, 1H, J= 3.41 Hz, H-1"), 5.48 (d,
1H, J= 1.82 Hz, H-1); 13C NMR (D2O, 75 MHz):δ 174.53, 174.20, 173.74,
145.74, 101.87, 97.44, 96.36, 84.26, 77.98, 75.30, 70.27, 68.04, 66.89,
64.04, 57.11, 54.77, 47.40, 45.85, 41.47, 41.14, 35.04, 27.86, 22.56,
22.36, 22.22, 21.19, 11.25.; Anal. for C27H47N5O10•15H2O. Calcd: C,
51.88; H, 8.02; N, 11.14. Found: C, 51.50; H, 8.13; N, 11.40.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, regioselective, optimized on solvent and reducing agent,
key step
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Efficient and Selective 1-N-Monoethylation of Sisomicin: Process
Development of Netilmicin
