$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-ethyl-N-(4-ethynylbenzyl)ethanamine (S14) Sodium triacetoxyborohydride
(1.22 g, 5.76 mmol) was added to a solution of 4-ethynylbenzaldehyde
(0.50 g, 3.8 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (20 mL) at rt. Diethylamine
(0.61 mL, 5.8 mmol) and acetic acid (0.12 mL) were then added under N2
atmosphere to the mixture at rt and the reaction was stirred for 18 h.
The reaction was quenched with sat. aq. NaHCO3 (10 mL) and the mixture
was stirred for 15 min. CH2Cl2 (20 mL) was then added and the layers were
separated. The aqueous layer was extracted using CH2Cl2 (10 mL), and the
combined organic layers were washed with brine and dried over Na2SO4. The
solvent was then removed in vacuo. The resultant oily residue was
purified by silica gel column chromatography using CH2Cl2/MeOH (0 to 10%)
gradient. N-ethyl-N-(4-ethynylbenzyl)ethanamine as pale yellow oil (0.45
g, 63%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.46 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.76 (d, J =
7.6 Hz, 2H), 3.78 (s, 2H), 3.08 (s, 1H), 2.72-2.66 (m, 4H), 1.13 (t, J =
7.2 Hz, 6H); LCMS (ESI) m/z calcd for [C13H17N + H]+ 188.14; found 187.9.
