$DATUM To a stirring solution of biaryl aniline 21 (4.49 g, 23.14 mmol) and
chloroacetaldehyde (2.18 g, 27.77 mmol) in 4 mL of 1:1 of 6M HCl:MeOH in
MeOH (60 mL) was added sodium cyanoborohydride (1.63 g, 25.92 mmol). The
reaction mixture was then stirred at rt for 5 days, concentrated, diluted
with methylene chloride and washed with NaHCO3, dried, concentrated and
chromatographed to yield 4.19 g (67%) of crude aminoalkyl chloride as a
solid: 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.79 (dd, J = 1.6, 1.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.74 (ddd, J =
7.7, 1.6, 1.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.55-7.45 (m, 2 H), 7.41 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 H),
6.74 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 H), 4.28 (br s, 1 H), 3.75 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 2 H),
3.57 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 2 H).
