$DATUM 5-(2-Chloroethylamino)-9H-quino[4,3,2-de][1,10]phenanthrolin-9-one (11)
and 5-Bis(2-chloroethylamino)-9Hquino[ 4,3,2-de][1,10]phenanthrolin-9-one
(12). NaBH3CN (0.63 g, 10 mmol) was added portionwise at 0 °C into a
solution of aminoascididemin 10 (1 g, 3.95 mmol) and chloroacetaldehyde
(50% in water, 2.6 mL, 16.8 mmol) in acetic acid (30 mL). The reaction
was maintained at 0 °C for 5 min and at room temperature for a further 30
min. The mixture was made alkaline by the addition of an NaHCO3-saturated
solution and extracted by CHCl3/MeOH 95:5. The organic layers were dried
over MgSO4 and concentrated. The crude product was purified by flash
chromatography (CHCl3 and then CHCl3/MeOH 99: 1) to give compounds 11 and
12. 5-(2-Chloroethylamino)-9H-quino[4,3,2-de][1,10]phenanthrolin-9-one
(11), yield (0.22 g, 18%) and 5-Bis(2-chloroethylamino)-9Hquino[
4,3,2-de][1,10]phenanthrolin-9-one (12), yield (0.14 g,10%) Compound 11.
Purple solid (0.22 g, 18%); mp 196 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 3.81 (t, 2H, J =
5.5 Hz); 3.88 (t, 2H, J = 5.5 Hz); 5.01 (br.s, 1H); 7.34 (dd, 1H, J = 8.8
and 2.5 Hz); 7.60 (d, 1H, J = 2.5 Hz); 7.65 (dd, 1H, J = 7.5 and 4.4 Hz);
8.41 (d, 1H, J = 5.8 Hz); 8.43 (d, 1H, J = 8.8 Hz); 8.82 (dd, 1H, J = 7.5
and 1.5 Hz); 9.15 (dd, 1H, J = 4.4 and 1.5 Hz); 9.21 (dd, 1H, J = 5.8
Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3): 42.83, 45.01, 100.76, 116.81, 118.78, 120.85,
125.38, 126.35, 129.35, 135.04, 136.04, 136.43, 140.22, 141.56, 148. IR
(CHCl3): 3427, 1672, 1620cm-1. tR was 5.22 min (98% purity) using system
I and 5.83 min (99% purity) using system II. Compound 12. Pink solid
(0.14 g,10%); mp 220 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ J = 4.4 and 3.83 (t, 4H, J =
7.0 Hz); 4.04 (t, 4H, J = 7.0 Hz); 7.47 (dd, 1H, J = 9.5 and 2.9 Hz);
7.66 (dd, 1H, J = 8.0 and 4.4 Hz); 7.70 (d, 1H, J = 2.9 Hz); 8.42 (d, 1H,
J = 5.6 Hz); 8.50 (d, 1H, J = 9.5 Hz); 8.81 (dd, 1H, J = 8.0 and 1.8 Hz);
9.16 (dd, 1H, J = 4.4 and 1.8 Hz); 9.23 (d, 1H, J = 5.6 Hz). 13C NMR
(CDCl3): δ 40.16, 53.60, 101.70, 116.60, 118.37, 118.68, 125.39, 125.91,
129.25, 135.13, 136.12, 136.38, 139.42, 141.93, 148.24, 148.73, 149.34,
152.22, 155.08, 181.43. IR (KBr): 1666; 1650 cm-1. tR was 3.39 min (97%
purity) using system I and 4.82 min (100% purity) using system II
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
