$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A. Reagents: 5b (0.45 g, 1.28 mmol),
O-benzylhydroxylamine hydrochloride (0.30 g, 1.95 mmol), ethanol (7 mL),
pyridine (5 mL), NaBH3CN (0.20 g, 3.12 mmol), methanol (16 mL), 37% HCl
(1.7 mL). A. Reductive aminotion. A solution of aldehyde (7e - 7i) and
O-benzylhydroxylamine hydrochloride (1-2 equiv) in a mixture of pyridine
and ethanol was stirred at room temperature for the time indicated below.
The reaction mixture was then evaporated, and thereafter co-evaporated
with toluene. The obtained crude product and NaBH3CN were dissolved in
methanol and the solution was stirred at rt for 30 minutes. After this
time the solution was cooled to 0 °C and 37% HCl was slowly added. The
mixture was then allowed to warm up to room temperature and stirred for 2
h. After the reaction was completed (TLC, ethyl acetate) the mixture was
basified by the addition of 10% NaOH (pH =12) and extracted with DCM. The
combined organic layers were dried, filtered and evaporated. B.
Acylation. The obtained crude material, triethylamine and acetyl chloride
in DCM were stirred at rt for 1-3 h. The reaction mixture was diluted
with water and the aqueous layer was extracted with DCM. The combined
organic fractions were dried over anhydrous MgSO4, filtered, then the
solvent was removed under vacuum and the sample purified by column
chromatography or used as a crude preparation. Reagents: 7d (0.23 g, 0.46
mmol), 10% Pd/C (0.02 g, 0.22 mmol), Na2CO3 (0.15 g, 1.38 mmol), THF (10
mL), ice-bath, time: 2.5 h, purification: preparative RP HPLC using
gradient elution (65 to 95% of methanol in 0.05% aqueous formic acid).
Diethyl 1-(2-bromophenyl)-3-(N-hydroxyacetamido)propylphosphonate (8d)
(13% from 5b, 0.02 g). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.60 (m, 2H), 7.39 (m,
1H), 7.19 (m, 1H), 4.11 (m, 2H), 3.88 (m, 3H), 3.63 (m, 1H), 3.33 (m,
1H), 2.43 (m, 1H), 2.24 (m, 1H), 2.04 (s, 3H), 1.32 (t, J= 7.0 Hz, 3H),
1.13 (t, J= 7.0 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.6, 136.0 (d, JC-P
= 6.6 Hz), 134.3, 130.7, 130.2, 129.0, 127.6, 64.3 (d, JC-P = 7.4 Hz),
64.0 (d, JC-P = 7.4 Hz), 46.3 (d, JC-P = 17.6 Hz), 40.9 (d, JC-P = 140.8
Hz), 28.0, 20.3, 16.7 (d, JC-P = 5.9 Hz), 16.5 (d, JC-P = 5.2 Hz); MS
(ESI+): m/z 408 (M+H+), 410 (M+2+H+); Formula: C15H23BrNO5P.
