$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of monomers Boc-aza-β3Leu-OH (2a, R =
CH2CH(CH3)2). To a solution of Nα-i-butyl-Nβ-Boc hydrazine 1a (1.88 g, 10
mmol) in methanol (20 mL) was added glyoxilic acid (2.22 g, 30 mmol) at
room temperature. After 30min of stirring, NaBH3CN (0.95 g, 15mmol) was
added in portions and the reaction mixture was stirred for 1 hr. Then, 2N
HCl was added to the solution until pH 1, followed by the addition of
NaHCO3 until pH 4. Finally, the solution was extracted twice by CH2Cl2
(20 mL). The organic layers were combined, dried with anhydrous Na2SO4
filtered and concentrated under reduced pressure to afford 2a as an oil
which crystallized slowly by the addition of diethyl ether. (2.21 g, 90
%). mp 63°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 0.88 (d, J = 6.6Hz, 6H, CH3), 1.38 (s, 9H,
t-Bu), 1.65 (m, 1H, CH), 2.58 (d, J = 7.0Hz, 2H, CH2), 3.54 (s, 2H, CH2),
5.99 (br, 1H, OH), 9.35 (br, 1H, NH). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 20.8 (q), 26.8
(d), 28.6 (q), 60.6 (t), 66.8 (t), 81.6 (s), 157.2 (s), 173.3 (s). HR-MS
m/z for C12H24N2O4 calcd 260.1736, obsd 260.1737.
