$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
monomers Boc-aza-β3Phe-OH (2c, R=CH2C6H5). The title compound was
synthesized from glyoxilic acid (2.22 g, 10 mmol) and Nα-benzyl-Nβ-Boc
hydrazine 1b (2.22 g, 10 mmol) following the general procedure for 2a.
(2.30g, 82 %); oil; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.46 (s, 9H, t-Bu), 3.63 (s, 2H,
CH2), 4.07 (s, 2H, CH2), 6.28 (br, 1H, NH), 7.46 (m, 5H, C6H5). 13C NMR
(CDCl3) 28.6 (q), 59.7 (t), 62.4 (t),81.3 (s),128.6 (d), 128.9 (d), 129.7
(d), 135.1 (s), 156.5 (s), 175.2 (s). HR-MS m/z for C14H20N2O4 calcd
280.1423, obsd 280.1422.
