$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of
3-(1′-Cyclobutylspiro[4H-1,3-benzodioxine-2,4′-piperidine]-6-yl)-5,5-dimethyl-1H-pyridazin-6-one
(8). A solution of 14 (285 g, 0.642 mol, 1.0 equiv), DMF (570 mL), MeOH
(2.9 L), HOAc (171 mL) and cyclobutanone (144 mL, 135 g, 1.93 mol, 3.0
equiv) was cooled to &lt;8 °C where sodium cyanoborohydride (202 g, 3.21
mol) was added portionwise over 30 min at &lt;10 °C. The batch was heated
to 59 °C for 1 h and cooled to 45 °C where it was concentrated in vacuo
(46 °C, 130 mm). The residue was partitioned between DI water (2.0 L) and
DCM (2.0 L) and the aqueous was taken to pH = 9 (concentrated aq K2CO3).9
The layers were separated and the organic phase was dried over Na2SO4,
filtered and concentrated in vacuo (40 mm hg, 40 °C) while exchanging the
solvent for MTBE (2.0 L). The precipitated product was collected by
vacuum filtration, washed with MTBE (500 mL) and dried overnight in a
vacuum oven at 55 °C to yield 8. 231 g (0.60 mol, 93.9%) off-white solid,
98.1 A% purity. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 10.72 (s, 1H), 7.57 (dd, J =
2.12, 8.6 Hz, 1H), 7.48 (d, J = 1.96 Hz, 1H), 6.85 (d, J = 8.64 Hz, 1H),
4.85 (s, 2H), 2.76 (s, 2H),2.73 (m, 1H), 2.33 (m, 4H), 1.95 (m, 2H), 1.83
(m, 6H), 1.61 (m, 2H), 1.06 (s, 6H).
