$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure C (Introduction of
Cyclobutyl on BasicNitrogen):
3-{Cyclobutyl[3-(5-fluoro-1H-indol-3-yl)propyl]-amino}-8-fluorochromane-5-carboxamide
(26). To 19 (0.14 g, 0.35 mmol) in anhydrous MeOH (6 mL) under nitrogen
at room temperature were added cyclobutanone (0.070 mL, 0.876 mmol),
acetic acid (0.050 mL, 0.84 mmol), and sodium cyanoborohydride (0.044 g,
0.70 mmol). The mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight. More
cyclobutanone (0.026 mL), acetic acid (0.21 mL), and sodium
cyanoborohydride (0.22 g) were added after 24 and 48 h, at which time the
reaction went to completion. Chromatography (5:4:1 EtOAc/hexane/MeOH (1%
NH4OH)) afforded 0.12 g (78%) of 26 as a sticky gum. Conversion to the
mono-HCl salt generated an off white solid.
(3R)-N-cyclobutyl-N-[3-(5-fluoro-1H-indol-3-yl)propyl]-5-methoxy-3,4-dihydro-2Hchromen-3-amine
(18a), yield 0.15 g (69%) as an off-white solid. mp 115 °C/dec; [α]D25 =
-33.02° (c = 1% SOLUTION, DMSO); 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 1.52 - 1.79
(m, 2 H), 1.91 - 2.45 (m, 6 H), 2.58 - 2.76 (m, 2 H), 2.78 -3.23 (m, 4
H), 3.68 - 3.90 (m, 4 H), 3.98 - 4.26 (m, 2 H), 4.32 - 4.48 (m, 1 H),
6.44 - 6.51 (m, 1 H), 6.57 - 6.65 (m, 1 H), 6.86 - 6.94 (m, 1 H), 7.09 -
7.16 (m, 1 H), 7.17 - 7.25 (m, 1 H), 7.26 - 7.36 (m, 2 H), 10.43 - 10.58
(m, 1 H), 10.94 (s, 1 H); MS (ES) m/z 409.2 ([M+H]+); Anal. (C25H29FN2O2
. HCl . 0.50 H2O) C,H,N.
