$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(Pyrrolidin-1-ylmethyl)benzonitrile (18). To a mixture of 17 (1.00 g,
7.63 mmol), pyrrolidine (630 μL, 7.63 mmol), and acetic acid (300 μL),
pic-BH3 (0.816 g, 7.63 mmol) was added over 5 min and the reaction
mixture was stirred at 25 °C for 3 h. Thereafter, 10% acetic acid was
added and the solution was stirred at 25 °C for 30 min. A saturated
solution of Na2CO3 was added, the aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl
acetate, and the combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried
over Na2SO4, and evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude product was
purified by silica gel flash chromatography (10% water in acetonitrile)
to afford 18. Pale yellow oil, yield 60%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.59
(d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.45 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 3.66 (s, 2H), 2.61-2.40
(m, 4H), 1.86-1.73 (m, 4H). MS (ESI) m/z 187 [M + H]+.
