$DATUM Dimethyl (S)-2-[N-(chloroacetyl)-N-(naphthalen-1-y)amino]butandioate
(17b) 2.HCl (1 g, 5.06 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 abs. (10 mL) and
triethylamine (0.74 mL, 5.06 mmol) and naphthalene-1-carbaldehyde (0.7
mL, 5.06 mmol) were added slowly. Then Na2SO4 was added and the mixture
was stirred for 16 h at room temperature. For work-up, the suspension was
filtered, the precipitate was washed with CH2Cl2 and the filtrate was
concentrated in vacuo. Diethyl ether was added to the resulting residue
and the mixture was filtered again. Evaporation of the filtrate gave the
imine 15b (1.3 g, 4.36 mmol) as a colorless oil, which was dissolved in
methanol (15 mL). After addition of NaBH4 (276.9 mg, 7.41 mmol) over 40
min under ice cooling, the mixture was stirred at room temperature for
another 5 min, before the solvent was evaporated in vacuo. Water (15 mL)
was added to the residue and the aqueous layer was extracted with diethyl
ether (5 x 10 mL). The combined organic layers were dried (K2CO3),
filtered and the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The oily
residue (16b, 1.14 g, 3.8 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 abs. (10 mL).
Triethylamine (0.42 mL, 3.04 mmol) and chloroacetyl chloride (0.48 mL,
6.07 mmol) were added dropwise under N2-atmosphere and ice cooling. The
mixture was stirred for 2.5 h at room temperature. The solvent was
removed in vacuo and diethyl ether (50 mL) was added to the resulting
residue. The suspension was filtered, washed and the filtrate was
concentrated in vacuo. Purification of the residue was performed. Pale
yellow oil, yield 1.11 g (58 % over 3 steps). fc (Φ 4 cm, h = 19 cm, v =
30 mL, cyclohexane/ethyl acetate = 4/1, Rf = 0.11). C19H2OClNO5, Mr =
377.8. HPLC (method ACN): tR = 19.9 min, purity 92.1 %. [α]D20 = -27.3 (c
= 1.07; EtOAc). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ [ppm] = 2.63 (dd, J = 17.0 / 7.0 Hz,
0.2H, CHCH2CO2CH3 NR), 2.79 (dd, J = 17.1 / 6.4 Hz, 0.8H, CHCH2CO2CH3
HR), 2.95 (dd, J = 17.0 / 7.0 Hz, 0.2H, CHCH2CO2CH3 NR), 3.29 (dd, J =
17.1 / 6.6 Hz, 0.8H, CHCH2CO2CH3 HR), 3.47 (s, 3 X0.2H, OCH3 NR), 3.58
(s, 3 X 0.2H, OCH3 NR, 3 X 0.8H, OCH3 HR), 3.71 (s, 3 X 0.8H, OCH3 HR),
4.07 (d, J = 12.8 Hz, 0.8H, O=CCH2ClHR), 4.12 (d, J = 12.8 Hz, 0.8H,
O=CCH2ClHR), 4.50 (s, broad, 2 x 0.2H, O=CCH2ClNR), 4.71 (t, J = 6.4 Hz,
0.8H, CHCH2CO2CH3 HR), 4.92 (d, J = 15.5 Hz, 0.2H, NCH2ArNR), 5.12 (t, J
= 7.0 Hz, 0.2H, CHCH2CO2CH3 NR), 5.19 (s, broad, 2 x 0.8H, NCH2ArHR),
5.26 (s, broad, 0.2H, NCH2ArNR), 7.20 (s, broad, 0.2H, Ar-HNR), 7.38 (t,
J = 7.8 Hz, 0.2H, Ar-HNR), 7.49 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 0.2H, Ar-HNR + 0.8H,
Ar-HHR), 7.54 - 7.62 (m, 0.2H, Ar-HNR + 3 x 0.8H, Ar- HHR), 7.77 (d, J =
8.1 Hz, 0.2H, Ar-HNR), 7.84 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 0.8H, Ar-HHR), 7.90 - 7.92
(m, 2 X 0.2H, Ar-HNR + 2 X 0.8H, Ar-HHR). Ratio of rotamers is 80:20. 13C
NMR (CD3OD): δ [ppm] = 34.3 (1C, CHCH2CO2CH3 NR), 34.5 (1C, CHCH2CO2CH3
HR), 41.3 (1C, O=CCH2ClNR), 41.4 (1C, O=CCH2ClHR), 50.5 (1C, NCH2ArNR),
50.8 (1C, NCH2ArHR), 52.1 (1C, OCH3 HR), 52.2 (1C, OCH3 NR), 52.3 (1C,
OCH3 NR), 52.8 (1C, OCH3 HR), 57.0 (1C, CHCH2CO2CH3 NR), 57.5 (1C,
CHCH2CO2CH3 HR), 122.3 (1C, Ar- CHR), 123.2 (1C, Ar-CNR), 124.4 (1C,
Ar-CHR), 124.6 (1C, Ar-CNR), 125.3 (1C, Ar-CNR), 125.5 (1C, Ar-CHR),
126.1 (1C, Ar-CNR), 126.4 (1C, Ar-CHR), 126.6 (1C, Ar-CNR), 126.9 (1C,
Ar-CHR), 127.1 (1C, Ar-CNR), 128.5 (1C, Ar-CNR), 129.0 (1C, Ar-CHR),
129.5 (1C, Ar-CHR), 130.6 (1C, Ar-Cq HR), 130.7 (1C, Ar-Cq HR), 131.0
(1C, Ar-Cq NR), 131.4 (1C, Ar-Cq NR), 133.2 (1C, Ar-Cq NR), 133.9 (1C,
Ar-Cq HR), 167.2 (1C, C=OHR), 167.9 (1C, C=ONR), 169.7 (1C, CO2CH3 HR),
169.9 (1C, CO2CH3 NR), 170.6 (1C, CO2CH3 NR), 171.7 (1C, CO2CH3 HR). MS
(EM, APCI): m/z = calcd. for C19H21ClNO5 378.1108 (M+H), found 378.1122.
IR (neat): ν [cm-1] = 2951 (C-H aliph.), 1732 (C=O ester), 1663 (C=O
amide), 795 (C-Cl), 737, 683 (arom. monosubst.).
