$DATUM Dimethyl (R)-2-[N-benzyN-(2-chloroacetyl)amino]butanedioate (ent-3)
ent-2.HCl (2 g, 10.1 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 abs. (25 mL) and
triethylamine (1.47 mL, 10.1 mmol) and freshly disted benzaldehyde (1 mL,
10.1 mmol) were added slowly. Then Na2SO4 was added and the mixture was
stirred for 16 h at room temperature. For work-up, the suspension was
filtered, the precipitate was washed with CH2Cl2 and the filtrate was
concentrated in vacuo. Diethyl ether was added to the resulting residue
and the mixture was filtered again. Evaporation of the filtrate gave the
imine ent-X (2.2 g, 8.8 mmol) as a colorless oil, which was dissolved in
methanol abs. (20 mL) and reduced directly by addition of NaBH4 (567 mg,
15.0 mmol) over 40 min under ice cooling. The mixture was stirred at room
temperature for another 5 min, before the solvent was evaporated in
vacuo. Water (20 mL) was added to the residue and the aqueous layer was
extracted with diethyl ether (5 x 10 mL). The combined organic layers
were dried (K2CO3), filtered and the solvent was removed under reduced
pressure. The oily residue (ent-Y, 1.9 g, 7.6 mmol) was dissolved in
CH2Cl2 abs. (20 mL). Triethylamine (0.84 mL, 6.04 mmol) and chloroacetyl
chloride (0.96 mL, 12.1 mmol) were added dropwise under N2- atmosphere
and ice cooling. The mixture was stirred for 2.5 h at room temperature.
The solvent was removed in vacuo and diethyl ether (50 mL) was added to
the resulting residue. The suspension was filtered, washed and the
filtrate was concentrated in vacuo. Purification of the residue was
performed. Colorless oil, yield 1.71 g, 52 % (over 3 steps). fc (Φ 5 cm,
h = 21 cm, v = 30 mL, cyclohexane/ethyl acetate = 4/1, Rf = 0.16).
C15H18ClNO5, Mr = 327.8. HPLC (method CAN): tR = 17.8 min, purity 96.6 %.
[α]D20 = +78.0 (c = 0.99; EtOAc). 13C NMR (CD3OD): δ [ppm] = 34.4 (1C,
CHCH2CO2CH3 HR), 34.5 (1C, CHCH2CO2CH3 NR), 41.4 (1C, O=CCH2ClHR), 42.0
(1C, O=CCH2ClNR), 47.5 (1C, NCH2ArNR), 52.2 (1C, OCH3 HR), 52.3 (1C, OCH3
NR), 52.7 (1C, OCH3 HR), 53.1 (1C, OCH3 NR), 53.5 (1C, NCH2ArHR), 57.4
(1C, CHCH2CO2CH3 NR), 57.5 (1C, CHCH2CO2CH3 HR), 127.5 (2C, Ar-CHR),
127.6 (2C, Ar- CNR), 128.4 (1C, Ar-CHR), 128.6 (2C, Ar-CNR), 129.1 (2C,
Ar-CHR), 129.8 (1C, Ar-CNR), 135.3 (1C, Ar-Cq HR), 137.1 (1C, Ar-Cq NR),
167.2 (1C, C=OHR), 167.9 (1C, C=ONR), 169.7 (1C, CO2CH3 HR), 169.9 (1C,
CO2CH3 NR), 170.6 (1C, CO2CH3 NR), 171.7 (1C, CO2CH3 HR). MS (EM, APCI):
m/z = calcd. for C15H19ClNO5 328.0951 (M+H), found 328.0982. 328.0982.
