$DATUM Dimethyl (S)-2-[N-benzyN-(2-chloroacetyl)amino]butanedioate (3) 2.HCl
(14.9 g, 75.4 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 abs. (150 mL) and
triethylamine (11 mL, 75.4 mmol) and freshly disted benzaldehyde (7.3 mL,
75.4 mmol) were added slowly. Then Na2SO4 was added and the mixture was
stirred for 16 h at room temperature. For work-up, the suspension was
filtered, the precipitate was washed with CH2Cl2 and the filtrate was
concentrated in vacuo. Diethyl ether was added to the resulting residue
and the mixture was filtered again. Evaporation of the filtrate gave the
imine (15.6 g, 62.6 mmol) as a colorless oil, which was dissolved in
methanol abs. (130 mL) and reduced directly by addition of NaBH4 (4 g,
106.4 mmol) over 40 min under ice cooling. The mixture was stirred at
room temperature for another 5 min, before the solvent was evaporated in
vacuo. Water (80 mL) was added to the residue and the aqueous layer was
extracted with diethyl ether (5 x 40 mL). The combined organic layers
were dried (K2CO3), filtered and the solvent was removed under reduced
pressure. The oily residue (12.7 g, 50.4 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2
abs. (100 mL). Triethylamine (5.6 mL, 40.3 mmol) and chloroacetyl
chloride (6.4 mL, 80.7 mmol) were added dropwise under N2-atmosphere and
ice cooling. The mixture was stirred for 2.5 h at room temperature. The
solvent was removed in vacuo and diethyl ether (180 mL) was added to the
resulting residue. The suspension was filtered, washed and the filtrate
was concentrated in vacuo. Purification of the residue was performed
Colorless oil, yield 12.2 g 49 % (over 3 steps). fc (Φ 8 cm, h = 19 cm, v
= 65 mL, cyclohexane/ethyl acetate = 7/3, Rf = 0.31). C15H18ClNO5, Mr =
327.8. HPLC (method ACN): tR = 18.0 min, purity 96.3 %. [α]D 20 = -64.8
(c = 0.99; EtOAc). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ [ppm] = 2.70 (dd, J = 17.3 / 6.5 Hz,
0.2H, CHCH2CO2CH3 NR), 2.73 (dd, J = 17.1 / 6.7 Hz, 0.8H, CHCH2CO2CH3
HR), 3.01 (dd, J = 17.3 / 6.5 Hz, 0.2H, CHCH2CO2CH3 NR), 3.28 (dd, J =
17.1 / 6.6 Hz, 0.8H, CHCH2CO2CH3 HR), 3.56 (s, 3 x 0.2H, OCH3 NR), 3.60
(s, 3 x 0.2H, OCH3 NR), 3.64 (s, 3 x 0.8H, OCH3 HR), 3.68 (s, 3 x 0.8H,
OCH3 HR), 4.06 (d, J = 12.6 Hz, 0.8H, O=CCH2ClHR), 4.11 (d, J = 12.7 Hz,
0.8H, O=CCH2ClHR), 4.24 (d, J = 15.5 Hz, 0.2H, NCH2ArNR), 4.46 (s, broad,
2 x 0.2H, O=CCH2ClNR), 4.51 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 0.8H, CHCH2CO2CH3 HR), 4.68
(d, J = 16.7 Hz, 0.8H, NCH2ArHR), 4.73 (d, J = 16.7 Hz, 0.8H, NCH2ArHR),
4.89 (d, J = 16.3 Hz, 0.2H, NCH2ArNR), 5.03 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 0.2H,
CHCH2CO2CH3 NR), 7.16 - 7.38 (m, 5H, Ar-HHR + NR). Ratio of rotamers is
80:20. MS (EI): m/z [%] = 329 (M, (Cl37), 10), 327 (M, (Cl35), 42), 91
(CH2Ar, 60). IR (neat): ν [cm-1] = 2952 (C-H aliph.), 1732 (C=O ester ),
1657 (C=O amide), 797 (C-Cl), 736, 699 (arom. monosubst.).
