$DATUM 4'-(Methylamino)-N-(tert-butyl)[1,1'-biphenyl]-2-sulfonamide (63). A
solution of 28 (2 g, 6.58 mmol) in ethylformate (30 mL) was refluxed for
2 h. The mixture was concentrated in vacuum to afford a formamide
intermediate (2.24 g) as a white solid. To a stirred solution of the
above formamide in THF (70 mL) at 0 °C was added LAH (1 M in THF, 20.25
mL, 20.3 mmol), and the resulting mixture was stirred at room temperature
for 3 h. The reaction was quenched with Et2O and water (1:1), filtered
through Celite, and purified by silica gel chromatography with CHCl3 to
63, yield 1.76 g, 48%. 1H NMR (CD3OD): δ 8.04 (dd, J = 8.0, J = 1.1 Hz,
1H), 7.56 (td, J = 7.7 Hz, J = 1.1 Hz, 1H), 7.43 (td, J = 7.7 Hz, J = 1.1
Hz, 1H), 7.30 (dd, J = 7.7 Hz, J = 1.1 Hz, 1H), 7.26 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H),
6.68 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 2.79 (s, 3H), 0.95 (s, 9H). LRMS 319 (M + H)+.
