$DATUM 2-(4-Methylbenzyl)hydrazinecarboxamide hydrochloride (22). Semicarbazide
HCl (40.00 g, 358.6 mmol, 1.00 equiv) and was slurried in EtOH (500 mL)
at rt. The ptolualdehyde (43.10 g, 358.60 mmol, 1.00 equiv) was added to
the mixture dropwise (exotherm from 21 °C to 30 °C noted). The reaction
was stirred overnight at rt and was concentrated via rotary evaporation
to a wet solid. EtOH (400 mL) was added and the mixture was concentrated
in vacuo to a thick solid. The solid was added to a slurry of 5% Pt/C
(50% water wet, 15 g) in EtOH (50 mL) and AcOH (150 mL). The system was
pressurized to 60 psi hydrogen gas and was heated to 50 °C for 3.5 h. The
slurry was filtered across Celite® filter aid, washing the cake with EtOH
(500 mL). The filtrate was cooled in an ice bath to 2 °C and was
filtered. The material was dried in vacuo to give the product (35.3 g,
46%) as a white solid, mp > 250 °C decomp.
2-(4-Methylbenzyl)hydrazinecarboxamide hydrochloride (22). Yield (35.3 g,
46%). 1H NMR (DMSO-d6): δ 2.27 (s, 3H), 4.14 (s, 2H), 6.52 (br s, 2H),
7.16 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H), 7.36 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H), 9.17 (br s, 1H),
10-12 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR (DMSO-d6): δ 21.4, 53.7, 128.4, 130.0 (2C),
131.8 (2C), 139.6, 157.9; IR (ATR): 3437, 3410, 3201, 3133, 2921, 2727,
2650, 1684, 1608 cm-1.
