$DATUM To a stirred solution of crude diamine (3.45 g, 13.53 mmol) and
cyclopentanone (1.40 mL, 16.23 mmol) in methylene chloride (35 mL) was
added sodium triacetoxyborohydride (5.74 g, 27.06 mmol), acetic acid
(1.55 mL, 27.06 mmol) and stirred at rt for 24 h. The reaction mixture
was quenched with 10% aqueous NaOH and extracted with methylene chloride.
The combined extracts were dried, concentrated and chromatographed over
silica gel (20 % EtOH/EtOAc) to yield 3.96 g (91%) of amine 6 as a white
solid: 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.17 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 H), 6.43 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2
H), 3.54 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1 H), 3.19 (m, 1 H), 2.94-2.90 (m, 2 H), 2.45
(m, 1 H), 2.11-1.98 (m, 4 H), 1.88-1.79 (m, 2 H), 1.71-1.31 (m, 8 H).
