$DATUM Ferrocenylamine 9 Ferrocene carboxaldehyde (9.3 mmol, 2 g, 1 eq.),
piperazine (46.5 mmol, 3.9 g, 5 eq.), and sodium triacetoxyborohydride,
NaBH(OAc)3 (23 mmol, 5 g, 2.5 eq.) were added to anhydrous THF (50 ml)
and stirred at room temperature for 24 h (Scheme 1), after which the
solvent was removed in vacuo. The residue was dissolved in EtOAc (50 ml),
basified to pH 10 with NaOH (1 M), and extracted with EtOAc (3 9 50 ml).
The combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4, and the solvent was
removed in vacuo. The residue was purified with CH2Cl2:MeOH (9:1, v/v)
and then with DCM:MeOH:NH4OH (25 %), (4:1:0.1, v/v/v). The pure compound
9 in 61 % yield. N-ferrocenyl-piperazine 9 The reaction of piperazine and
ferrocene carboxaldehyde afforded a yellow oil; yield: 0.71 g (61 %). mp:
120.1-122.6°C; IR (ATR) νmax/cm-1: 3260, 3070, 2928, 2802, 1451, 1328,
1280, 1136, 1104, 1059, 1037, 1023, 1′′1, 908, 811, 594; 1H NMR (600 MHz,
CDCl3) δ ppm: 4.14 (t, J = 1.9 Hz, 2H, H-3a), 4.08 (s, 7H, H-2a and
H-4a), 3.34 (s, 2H, H-1b), 2.86 (t, J = 5.0 Hz, 4H, H-2b), 2.39 (s, 4H,
H-3b); 13C NMR (151 MHz, CDCl3) δ ppm: 82.12 (C-1a), 70.31 (C-3a), 68.48
(C-4a), 68.08 (C-2a), 58.77 (C-1b), 53.17 (C-3b), 45.48 (C-2b); HRMS
(APCI) m/z [M]+: 284.0965 (Calcd. for C15H20FeN2: 284.0975).
