$DATUM 4-((4-(Oxetan-3-yl)piperazin-1-yl)sulfonyl)benzonitrile (54). A solution
of 53 (2.5 g, 9.95 mmol), oxetan-3-one (1.4 g, 19.4 mmol), and
titanium(IV) isopropoxide (3.1 g, 10.9 mmol) in EtOH (50 mL) was stirred
at 60 °C for 2 h. Sodium cyanoborohydride (2.5 g, 39.7 mmol) was then
added, and the reaction mixture was stirred at 60 °C for an additional 12
h. The mixture was cooled to 25 °C and was concentrated under vacuum. The
residue was diluted with CH2Cl2 (100 mL), and the resulting solution was
washed sequentially with water (2 × 100 mL) and brine (1 × 100 mL). The
organic layer was dried over Na2SO4 and was concentrated under vacuum.
The residue was purified on a silica gel column and eluted with
EtOAc/petroleum ether (80:20). 54 (1.6 g, 44%) as a white solid. LCMS
(method 4, ESI): t R = 1.03 min, m/z = 308.0 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Fragment-based identification of amides derived from
