$DATUM 1-Ethyl-3-(4-((6S,9R)-4-((S)-3-methylmorpholino)-10-(oxe- To a solution
of crude 7 (276 mg, 0.654 mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (5.2 mL) was added
3-oxetanone (240 mg, 3.3 mmol) and the reaction mixture was stirred under
nitrogen for 10 min at 70 °C. Sodium triacetoxyborohydride (440 mg, 2.1
mmol) was then added and the reaction mixture was stirred for 90 minutes.
The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature and quenched by the
addition of water and then saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate. The
mixture was extracted with DCM (2×). The combined organic layers were
dried over sodium sulfate and concentrated in vacuo. The crude residue
was purified by flash column chromatography (0−80% EtOAc/heptane, then
0−10% MeOH/DCM) to provide the desired product which was further purified
by chiral SFC to give the title compounds as pure diastereomers.
1-Ethyl-3-(4-((6S,9R)-4-((S)-3-methylmorpholino)-10-(oxetan-3-yl)-6,7,8,9-tetrahydro-5H-6,9-epiminocyclohepta[d]-pyrimidin-2-yl)phenyl)urea
(20). The title compound was prepared in a manner analogous to that for
11 to give the title compound as a pure diastereomer. 48.2 mg, 18% yield.
1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 8.60 (s, 1H), 8.20−8.09 (m, 2H), 7.49−7.38
(m, 2H), 6.14 (t, J = 5.5 Hz, 1H), 4.65 (t, J = 6.3 Hz, 1H), 4.56 (t, J =
6.1 Hz, 1H), 4.46−4.37 (m, 2H), 4.13−4.07 (m, 1H), 3.88−3.75 (m, 4H),
3.69−3.57 (m, 3H), 3.55−3.50 (m, 1H), 3.34−3.30 (m, 1H), 3.17−3.08 (m,
2H), 3.00 (dd, J = 16.3, 4.9 Hz, 1H), 2.18 (d, J = 16.4 Hz, 1H),
2.15−2.08 (m, 1H), 2.07−1.98 (m, 1H), 1.76−1.67 (m, 1H), 1.48−1.40 (m,
1H), 1.34 (d, J = 6.7 Hz, 3H), 1.06 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H). LCMS, m/z = 479
[M + H]+. Cystal Data: Empirical formula C26H34N6O3 Formula weight 478.59
Temperature 100(2) K Wavelength 1.54178 Å Crystal system Monoclinic Space
group C2 Unit cell dimensions a = 27.2948(5) Å, b = 15.3732(3) Å, c =
18.4555(4) Å; α= 90°, β= 132.5200(10)°, γ = 90° Volume 5707.7(2) Å3 Z 8
Crystal size 0.06 x 0.04 x 0.02 mm3.
