$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the Reductive Alkylation
of 1-tert-Butyloxycarbonylpiperazine: 4-Cyclobutylpiperazine-1-carboxylic
Acid tert-Butyl Ester. To a solution of 1-tert-butyloxycarbonylpiperazine
(2.24 g, 12.0 mmol) in THF (20 mL) were added water (0.2 mL),
cyclobutanone (1.35 mL, 18.1 mmol), AcOH (2.20 mL), and NaCNBH3 (18 mL, 1
M in THF, 18 mmol). The mixture was stirred at 60 °C overnight and
concentrated, and the residue was mixed with water (50 mL) and aqueous
HCl (1 M, 15 mL). The solution was washed with AcOEt (2 x 30 mL), made
basic by addition of K2CO3, and extracted (2 x 20 mL AcOEt), and the
combined extracts were washed with brine, dried with MgSO4, and
concentrated. The title compound (1.1 g, 38%) was obtained as a colorless
oil, which was used without further purification.
4-(1-Propylbutyl)piperazine-1-carboxylic acid tert-butyl ester: oil. 1H
NMR (DMSO-d6) δ 0.86 (t, J = 7 Hz, 6H), 1.12 (m, 2H), 1.28 (m, 4H), 1.39
(m, 11H), 2.38 (m, 4H), 2.59 (m, 1H), 3.25 (m, 4H).
