$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Ethyl 2-(2-Fluoro-4-iodoanilino)acetate (41h).
To a solution of 40 (100 mg, 0.4 mmol) in EtOH (10 mL) at 0 °C were added
c-HCl (0.1 mL) and ethyl glyoxylate (0.17 mL, 0.8 mmol). The reaction
mixture was stirred for 30 min at ambient temperature, and sodium
cyanoborohydride (55.6 mg, 0.8 mmol) was added. The resulting reaction
mixture was extracted with EtOAc, and the combined organic layers were
washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification of the residue by flash column chromatography
(EtOAc:n-hexane ) 1:10) afforded 133 mg (98%) of 41h:
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
