$DATUM 1-[4-(3-Chloropropoxy)benzyl]piperidine (10).29 To a solution of aldehyde
9 (2.50 g, 12.6 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and piperidine (1.4 mL, 14 mmol, 1.1
equiv) in dichloroethane (50 mL) was added sodium triacetoxyborohydride
(3.73 g, 17.7 mmol, 1.4 equiv). After 15 h, the resulting mixture was
treated with 10% aqueous sodium hydroxide (50 mL). The aqueous phase was
extracted with DCM (2 x 50 mL), and the combined organic phases were
dried (MgSO4) and evaporated, giving the title compound as a colorless
oil that was used without further purification (3.05 g, 90%)
1-[4-(3-Chloropropoxy)benzyl]piperidine (10), yield 3.05 g, 90% 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 7.22 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 6.84 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 4.10 (t, J
= 5.9 Hz, 2H), 3.74 (t, J = 6.3 Hz, 2H), 3.41 (s, 2H), 2.40-2.30 (br s,
4H), 2.26-2.19 (m, 2H), 1.59-1.52 (m, 4H), 1.46-1.38 (m, 2H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3) δ 157.6, 130.8, 130.4, 114.0, 64.2, 63.2, 54.3, 41.5, 32.3, 25.9,
24.4.
