$DATUM 1,1-Dimethylethyl 4-(3-cyclopenten-1-yl)-3-oxo-1-piperazinecarboxylate. A
mixture of 1-amino-3-cyclopentene hydrochloride (6.25 g, 51.2 mmol),
methyl N-{[(1,1-dimethylethyl)oxy]carbonyl}-N-(2- oxoethyl)glycinate
(10.5 g, 42.7 mmol, see Mendez-Andino, et al, Bioorganic and Medicinal
Chemistry, 2007, 15, 2092), DIPEA (8.95 mL, 51.2 mmol), and sodium
sulfate (36.4 g, 256 mmol) in MeOH (170 mL) was stirred at RT for 2 hours
and then treated with sodium borohydride (1.96 g, 51.2 mmol) added in
portions. After another 2 hours the mixture was treated with 60%
NaH/mineral oil (3.41 g, 85.0 mmol) in portions. After 1.5 hours the
mixture was slowly diluted with 10% aqueous citric acid to a pH of
approximately 5.0. The resulting mixture was extracted with EtOAc (3x).
The combined EtOAc extracts were washed with brine, dried over sodium
sulfate, and concentrated at reduced pressure to afford a brown oil. The
crude material was purified by flash chromatography (silica gel, 0-45%
EtOAc/hexane). (6.70 g, 59%) as an off-white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 5.75 (s, 2H), 5.44 - 5.54 (m, 1H), 4.09 (s, 2H), 3.59 (t, J =
5.17 Hz, 2H), 3.20 (t, J = 5.17 Hz, 2H), 2.71 (dd, J = 8.98, 15.80 Hz,
2H), 2.19 - 2.30 (m, 2H), 1.47 (s, 9H).
