$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Immediately, the residue was diluted with anhydrous THF (2.0 mL),
piperidine (18.1 μL, 0.309 mmol) was added followed by NaBH(OAc)3 (195.8
mg, 0.924 mmol) at room temperature under N2. The reaction mixture was
then stirred at room temperature under N2 for 1 day. The mixture was
cooled to 0 °C, poured into ice-cooled water (20 mL), and then the
resulting mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (20 mL × 2). The organic
layers were combined, dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and concentrated in
vacuo. PTLC purification (silica gel, CH2Cl2/MeOH/25% aqueous ammonia =
15:1:0.1) was performed.
1'-[3-(piperidin-1-yl)propyl]spiro[indene-1,4'-piperidine] (10). 1H NMR
(270 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.39-7.16 (4H, m, Ar H), 6.85 (1H, d, J= 5.62 Hz,
CH═CH), 6.74 (1H, d, J= 5.62 Hz, CH═CH), 3.06-2.98 (2H, m, CH2),
2.51-1.34 (22H, m, CH2). MS (ESI positive) m/z: [M+H]+ 311. Anal.
(C21H30N2·C6H8O7) C, H, N. hNOP receptor binding Ki (nM): 21.7; hNOP
receptor binding Ki (nM): >450. Antagonism against N/OFQ-stimulated [35S]
GTPcS binding IC50 (nM): 218. Half-life in HLM: 13 minutes. Size (MW):
310.48.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient design, synthesis and structure-activity relationship studies
of 1-(3'-substituted propyl)-4-arylpiperidines as non-peptide antagonists
of nociceptin/orphanin FQ receptor: biological activities, metabolic
stabilities and hERG channel bindings
