$DATUM {4-[2-(5-Methyl-2-phenyl-oxazol-4-yl)-ethoxy]-benzylamino}-acetic acid
methyl ester (6). A mixture of glycine methyl ester hydrochloride (2.4 g,
19.1 mmol), aldehyde 5 (4.52 g, 14.7 mmol), Et3N (2.92 mL, 20.95 mmol),
4Å molecular sieves (0.5 g), and anhydrous MgSO4 (2 g) in MeOH (85 mL)
was stirred at 25 °C for 12 h. The reaction mixture was then cooled to 0
°C and solid NaBH4 (0.72 g, 19 mmol) was added in portions. The reaction
mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 0.5 h and at 25 °C for 3 h, after which
it was quenched with 10% aq. NaHCO3 (55 mL). After stirring for 15 min,
the mixture was concentrated in vacuo, diluted with 50 mL H2O and
extracted with EtOAc (100 mL x 3). The combined organic extracts were
washed with brine, dried (MgSO4), evaporated under reduced pressure and
the residue was chromatographed (SiO2; 3:1 to 1:1 hexanes:EtOAc) to
afford amino-ester 6 (4.48 g, 80%) as a pale yellow solid.
{4-[2-(5-Methyl-2-phenyl-oxazol-4-yl)-ethoxy]-benzylamino}-acetic acid
methyl ester (6), yield (4.48 g, 80%) 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 2.37 (s,
3H, oxazole-CH3), 2.97 (t, 2H, J = 6.5 Hz, -CH2CH2OAr), 3.39 (s, 2H,
-CH2CO2Me), 3.92 (s, 5H, ArCH2N + OCH3), 4.23 (t, 2H, -CH2CH2OAr), 6.86
(d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 7.22 (d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 7.37-7.45 (m, 3H),
7.96-7.98 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 10.2, 26.4, 49.8, 51.7,
52.7, 66.8, 114.5, 125.9, 127.8, 128.6, 129.4, 129.7, 131.6, 132.7,
145.0, 158.0, 159.5, 172.9. CHN: Calculated for C22H24N2O4: C 69.46, H
6.36, N 7.36; Found: C 69.35, H 6.64, N 7.38. IR (KBr): 2700-3100 (w,
br), 1740 (vs), 1512, 1245, 1175 cm-1. UV (CH2Cl2; 13.5 mg/L): λmax 282,
304 (sh), 290 (sh) nm. LRMS (M + H+): 381.001; HRMS: Calculated for
C22H25N2O4: 381.1814, found: 381.1811.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM molecular sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
