$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(4-bromo-2,6-difluorobenzyl)morpholine (S11) Sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (1.44 g, 6.8 mmol) was added to a solution of
4-bromo-2,6-difluorobenzaldehyde (1.0 g, 4.5 mmol) in DCE (20 mL) at rt.
Morpholine (0.59 mL, 6.8 mmol) and acetic acid (0.1 mL) were then added
under N2 atmosphere to the mixture at rt and the reaction was stirred for
18 h. The reaction was quenched with sat. aq. NaHCO3 (10 mL) and the
mixture was stirred for 15 min. Dichloromethane (20 mL) was then added
and the layers were separated. The aqueous layer was extracted using DCM
(10 mL), and the combined organic layers were washed with brine and dried
over Na2SO4. The solvent was then removed in vacuo. The resultant oily
residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography using
CH2Cl2/MeOH (100 to 90:10) gradient.
4-(4-bromo-2,6-difluorobenzyl)morpholine as a pale yellow oil (1.3 g,
98%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.09 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 2H), 3.69 (d, J =
4.4 Hz, 4H), 3.63 (s, 2H), 2.49 (bm, 4H); LCMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
[C11H12BrF2NO+ H]+ 292.1; found 293.0.
