$DATUM To a solution of aldehyde (3.0 g, 6.52 mmol) was added morpholine (681.0
mL, 7.82 mmol) and NaBH(OAc)3 (2.21 g, 10.42 mmol) and the mixture was
kept stirring for 9h. NaHCO3 (sat. aq) was added and the organic layer
separated and washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and
concentrated. The product was purified by column
(ethylacetate/CH2Cl2/MeOH; 10:10:1).
(S)-1-methyl-N-(4-((2-(2-morpholinoethyl)piperidin-1-yl)sulfonyl)phenyl)-3-(trifluoromethyl)-1H-pyrazole-5-carboxamide
(2o) as a white solid, yield 2.8 g, 81%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 8.18
(s, 1H), 7.74-7.80 (m, 2H), 7.65-7.72 (m, 2H), 7.05 (s, 1H), 4.25 (s,
3H), 4.04-4.11 (m, 1H), 3.76 (dd, J = 4.1, 14.3 Hz, 1H), 3.67 (t, J = 4.5
Hz, 1H), 2.97-3.08 (m, 1H), 2.23-2.45 (m, 6H), 1.78-1.90 (m, 1H),
1.55-1.66 (m, 1H), 1.30-1.53 (m, 5H). LC-MS (ESI) (LCT, 3 min) Rt 0.57
min; greater than 95% purity at λ 254 and 210 nm. MS: m/z 530.2 [M + 1].
Anal. calcd for C23H30F3N5O4S•H2O: C, 50.45; H, 5.89; N, 12.79. Found: C,
50.98; H, 5.72; N, 12.74.
