$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of tert-butyl
3-aminoazetidine-1-carboxylate 4 (General Procedure) Method A To a
solution of 1-Boc-3-azetidinone 3 in methylene chloride (100 mL) at room
temperature under Ar atmosphere was added sequentially aniline (14 mmol),
acetic acid (1.4 mmol) and sodium triacetoxyborohydride (42 mmol). The
reaction mixture was stirred at the same temperature for 5 h. To the
resulting reaction mixture was added 1N aqueous NaOH solution while
stirring. This mixture was stirred at room temperature for 0.5 h and then
extracted with methylene chloride. The organic extract was dried over
anhydrous MgSO4. The solvent was removed by evaporation and the crude
product was then purified by flash chromatography on silica gel
(n-hexane:ethyl acetate = 1:1) to obtain 4 (R1=phenyl or substitutied
phenyl group) (soild, 49~95% yields). Synthesis of the azetidine
derivatives 7 (series A) (General Procedure) path A (n=1) To a solution
of 4 (1.0 mmol) in DMF (6.0 mL) at room temperature was added alkyl or
benzyl halide 5 (1.5 mol) and K2CO3 (3.0 mol). The mixture was refluxed
for 6 h and the reaction mixture was then cooled to room temperature. The
solvent was removed by evaporation and the residue was dissolved in ethyl
acetate, washed with water, and then dried over MgSO4. The solvent was
removed by evaporation and the crude product was then purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel (n-hexane:ethyl acetate = 4:1) to obtain 7
(n=1) (oil, 41~99% yields). Synthesis of the azetidine derivatives 8
(series A) (General Procedure) - Use of trifluoroacetic acid To a
solution of 7 (0.5 mmol) dissolved in methylene chloride (10 mL) at room
temperature was added trifluoroacetic acid (6.5 mmol). The reaction
mixture was stirred for 10 h. To the resulting reaction mixture was added
1N aqueous NaOH solution (1.0 mL) while stirring. This mixture was
stirred at room temperature for 0.5 h and then extracted with methylene
chloride. The organic extract was dried over anhydrous MgSO4. The solvent
was removed by evaporation and the crude product was then purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel (methylene chloride:methanol = 4:1) to
obtain the 3-aminoazetidines 8, series A (26~96% yields).
N-(azetidin-3-y)-N-benzylcyclohexanamine (10cz) Yield 77%; oil. 1H NMR
(400MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.07-1.85 (m, 10H, cyclohexyl H), 2.42 (m, 1H,
cyclohexyl C1H), 2.71-2.80 (m, 3H, CH, CHCH2), 3.27 (m, 2H, azetidine H),
3.57 (m, 2H, azetidine H), 3.60 (s, 2H, NCH2), 7.21-7.33 (m, 5H, ArH);
13C NMR (100MHz, CDCl3) δ 26.19, 26.43, 28.92, 32.81, 50.23, 54.85,
57.79, 60.35, 126.43, 126.66, 128.05, 128.13, 128.61, 147.51.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
