$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure H: To a stirred solution of
an acid (1.0 equivalent) in THF (concentration ~1-2M) at 0°C was added
NMM (1.0 equivalent). The solution was stirred for 5 min then IBCF (1.0
equivalent) was added. The solution was stirred for 10 min before the
amine (1.2-2.0 equivalents) was added. The reaction was allowed to return
to room temperature and stirred for 18 h. THF was removed under reduced
pressure and EtOAc was added. The organic layer was washed with saturated
aqueous NH4Cl then with saturated aqueous NaHCO3. The organic layer was
dried (Na2SO4 or MgSO4), filtered and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The crude material was purified by flash column chromatography
on silica gel or by recrystallization. General Procedure B. The
BOC-protected amine was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (∼4 mL/mmol), and
trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) (∼2 mL/mmol) was added. The mixture was
stirred at room temperature for 0.5-5 h. In a standard workup, the
mixture was neutralized with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 or 1 N NaOH, and
the aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined extracts were
dried (Na2SO4 or MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The crude material was used in the next reaction as is or was
purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel. To a solution of
(R)-2-amino-N-(t-butyl)-2-phenylacetamide (1.94 g, 9.40 mmol) in dry THF
was added BH3.THF (37.0 ml of 1 M in THF, 37.6 mmol). This solution was
stirred at 60°C for 18 h. The reaction mixture was then cooled to room
temperature. MeOH (10 ml) was added dropwise, and then 6 N HCl (10 ml)
was added. The mixture was stirred at 60°C for 1 h then the mixture was
concentrated under reduced pressure. CH2Cl2 (100 ml), saturated aqueous
NaHCO3 (100 ml) and 10 N NaOH (4 ml) were added. The aqueous layer was
extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 100 ml) and the combined organic extracts were
dried (MgSO4), filtered and concentrated under reduced pressure. (R)-N
1-(t-butyl)-2-phenylethane-1,2-diamine 13b (1.63 g, 90%) was used in the
next step without further purification.
N1-cyclohexyl-2-(pyridin-3-yl)ethane-1,2-diamine 13a (R1=3-pyridine, R2=
c-Hex) was prepared using the same chemistry as
(R)-1-(t-butyl)-4-phenyl-3-(piperidin-4-yl)imidazolidin-2-one (10b;
R1=Ph, R2=t-Bu) except that cyclohexylamine was used in lieu of
t-butylamine.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
