$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (R)-methyl 1-cyclohexylpyrrolidine-2-carboxylate (33). D-proline
methylester hydrochloride (0.346 g, 2.09 mmol), triethylamine (233 μL,
1.67 mmol) and cyclohexanone (217 μL, 2.09 mmol) were dissolved in dry
MeOH (7 mL), activated molecular sieves (3Å) were added, and the solution
was stirred for 5 minutes under N2. A solution of 1.25 M HCl in MeOH (400
μL, 0.50 mmol) and NaBH3CN (0.110 g, 1.75 mmol) were added to the
solution and the mixture stirred for 1.5 hours. The reaction was
filtered, the solvent evaporated under reduced pressure and the residue
extracted with AcOEt/NaHCO3 sat. which was used without further
purification a colorless oil (0.485 g, quantitative yield). 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 3.70 (s, 3H), 3.47 (dd, J1 = 9 Hz, J2 = 4 Hz, 1H),
3.18-3.09 (m, 1H), 2.67-2.56 (m, 1H), 2.43-2.31 (m, 1H), 2.14-2.00 (m,
1H), 1.97-1.67 (m, 7H), 1.64-1.53 (m, 1H), 1.31-1.04 (m, 5H) ; 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 75 MHz) δ 175.8 (C), 62.3 (CH), 61.1 (CH), 51.5 (CH), 50.1 (CH2),
31.5 (CH2), 30.5 (CH2), 29.9 (CH2), 25.8 (CH2), 25.1 (CH2), 23.3 (CH2);
MS (ESI+) m/z 211.3 ([[M+1]+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM mol. sieves used
