$DATUM 4-((Benzylamino)methyl)-N,N-diethylaniline (S2). Methol 2: The mixture of
3.5 g (0.020 mol) 4-N,N-diethylaminobenzaldehyde and 2.2 g (0.020 mol)
benzylamine was heated to 100 °C for 2 h. After cooled, methanol 20 mL
and NaBH4 3.8 g (0.10 mol) was added to the mixture. The reactant was
stirred for 12 hrs and then poured into water, extracted with EA. The
organic layer was dried with anhydrous K2CO3, filtered and concentrated
in vacuo. The residue was purified by chromatography (EA/Hexane 2:1, 100
mL silica gel) to give product. Liquid 4.6 g (0.017 mol, yeild 85). 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.32 (m, 4H), 7.21(m, 3H), 6.64 (d, J = 8.0 Hz,
2H), 4.53 (s, 1H), 3.79 (s, 2H), 3.69 (s, 2H), 3.34 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 4H),
1.15 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 6H).
