$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4-((Benzylamino)methyl)-N,N-diethylaniline
(S2). Methol 2: The mixture of 3.5 g (0.020 mol)
4-N,N-diethylaminobenzaldehyde and 2.2 g (0.020 mol) benzylamine was
heated to 100 °C for 2 h. After cooled, methanol 20 mL and NaBH4 3.8 g
(0.10 mol) was added to the mixture. The reactant was stirred for 12 hrs
and then poured into water, extracted with EA. The organic layer was
dried with anhydrous K2CO3, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The
residue was purified by chromatography (EA/Hexane 2:1, 100 mL silica gel)
to give product. 4-((Benzylamino)methyl)-N,N-dimethylaniline (S3).
Compound S3 was prepared from benzylamine and
4-N,N-dimethylaminobenzaldehyde using method 2. Yield 83%. 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.36 (m, 4H), 7.26 (m, 1H), 7.25 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 6.74
(d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 3.83 (s, 2H), 3.75 (s, 2H), 2.95 (s, 6H).
