$DATUM 2-Trifluoromethyl-4-(3-endo-benzylamino-8-azabicyclo[3.2.1]oct-8-yl)benzonitrile
13 3 To a solution of 12 (3.08 g, 10.47 mmol, 1.0 equiv.) in CH2Cl2 (45
mL) with molecular sieves (0.5 g, 3 Å) actetic acid (0.9 mL, 15.71 mmol,
1.5 equiv.) and benzylamine (1.14 mL, 10.47 mmol, 1.0 equiv.) were added.
After 5 min of stirring NaHB(OAc)3 (3.33 g, 15.71 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was
added and the mixture was stirred for 45 h at RT. CH2Cl2 (50 mL) was
added to the mixture and this was extracted once with aq. NaOH solution
(1 N, 250 mL). The aqueous layer was extracted twice with CH2Cl2 (50 mL).
The combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and evaporated. The
resulting orange solid was washed with MeOH (0 °C) and dried in vacuo. 13
(2.66 g, 66%) as a slightly yellow solid. R f = 0.26 (heptane/EtOAc 1:2);
M.p. = 144.4-145.2 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD): δ = 1.68 (d, J = 14.9,
2H, H-C2', H-C4'), 2.04-2.12 (m, 4H, H-C2', H-C4', H-C6', H-C7'),
2.28-2.44 (m, 2H, H-C6', H-C7'), 2.74-2.86 (m, 1H, H-C3'), 3.75 (s, 2H,
H-C1''), 4.37 (b, 2H, HC1', H-C5'), 6.99 (dd, J = 8.8, 2.5, 1H, H-C5),
7.07 (d, J = 2.4, 1H, H-C3), 7.16-7.35 (m, 5H, H-C3'', H-C4'', H-C5'',
H-C6'', H-C7''), and 7.62 (dd, J = 8.8, 0.5, 1H, H-C6) ppm; 13C NMR (126
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 28.6, 32.9, 50.5, 52.9, 54.0, 94.1, 111.3 (q, 3 J CF =
4.9), 115.6, 117.5, 122.9 (q, 1 J CF = 274.2), 128.2, 128.6, 129.0, 134.6
(q, 2 J CF = 31.7), 136.4, and 148.8 ppm; IR (ATR): 3313, 2951, 2220,
1653, 1608, 1559, 1516, 1506, 1452, 1388, 1368, 1284, 1269, 1162, 1123,
1040, 1010, 962, 861, 820, 734, and 703 cm-1.
